# Legal Consultant — shared guardrails for OpenAI Codex CLI

> Generated by `scripts/build-runtimes.py` from the plugin `CLAUDE.md` templates; do not edit. Regenerate with `python3 scripts/build-runtimes.py`.

Legal Consultant is a jurisdiction-pluggable fork of Anthropic's `claude-for-legal`. Under Claude Code the shared guardrails live in each plugin's `CLAUDE.md`; OpenAI Codex CLI does not read those files, so they are reproduced here and apply to every `commercial-legal-*`, `corporate-legal-*`, and `employment-legal-*` skill.

## Runtime rules

- **Practice profile path.** `${LEGAL_CONSULTANT_HOME:-~/.legal-consultant}/<plugin>/CLAUDE.md` for `commercial-legal`, `corporate-legal`, `employment-legal`, plus the shared `${LEGAL_CONSULTANT_HOME:-~/.legal-consultant}/company-profile.md`. Any text that still says `~/.claude/plugins/config/claude-for-legal/<plugin>/…` means this path. If a populated profile exists only at the old path, copy it forward once, then use the new path.
- **Jurisdiction tree.** The `legal-consultant-jurisdictions` skill carries `references/jurisdictions/`. Skills resolve the profile's jurisdiction codes against `REGISTRY.md` and load `<code>/MANIFEST.md`, `INDEX.md`, and the instrument files. Unpopulated code: stop.
- **Primary-source research.** For a non-`usa` code use the portal named in the manifest, e.g. `python3 scripts/fetch-law.py --portal boe --id <guid> --lang ar` (the script is under the jurisdiction skill's `scripts/` folder when installed from this repo) or `curl` of the portal page; the built-in web-fetch tool rejects the laws.boe.gov.sa TLS chain. Tag `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[BOE — official English]`. On failure, apply the no-silent-supplement rule.
- **Sandbox and network (Codex).** The `read-only` sandbox has no network (`CODEX_SANDBOX_NETWORK_DISABLED=1`): the fetch script and any piped `curl` fail with "Could not resolve host", so every research step ends in a stopped run. Run this plugin's skills with `codex exec -s workspace-write -c sandbox_workspace_write.network_access=true` (or the equivalent config). Inside the sandbox curl cannot reach the macOS Keychain, so the portal's incomplete certificate chain fails verification; `scripts/fetch-law.py` retries with the public DigiCert chain in `scripts/certs/boe-chain.pem` and succeeds. Probe the portal with a GET, never `curl -I`: the portal redirects HEAD requests into a loop.
- **Not available in this runtime.** Claude Code subagents (`agents/*.md`), hooks, and scheduled agents have no direct equivalent here; the scheduled behaviours (renewal watcher, leave tracker, deal debrief, playbook monitor, data-room watcher) are run on demand by invoking the matching skill. See `docs/runtime-matrix.md`.
- **MCP servers.** Configure connectors in `~/.codex/config.toml` under `[mcp_servers.<name>]`. None are required for the jurisdiction files; the upstream legal-research connectors (CourtListener, Westlaw) are only relevant when `usa` is in the footprint.

## Skills

- `$commercial-legal-amendment-history` — Trace how a contract has changed across its base agreement and all amendments — either a summary of all changes over time, or a provision trace for a specific c
- `$commercial-legal-cold-start-interview` — Run the cold-start interview to learn your commercial contracts practice and write your team practice profile
- `$commercial-legal-customize` — Guided customization of your commercial contracts practice profile — change one thing without re-running the whole cold-start interview
- `$commercial-legal-escalation-flagger` — Route a contract issue to the right approver per the escalation matrix in `${LEGAL_CONSULTANT_HOME:-~/.legal-consultant}/commercial-legal/CLAUDE.md`, and draft 
- `$commercial-legal-matter-workspace` — Manage matter workspaces — new, list, switch, close, or detach (practice-level)
- `$commercial-legal-nda-review` — Reference: fast triage of inbound NDAs into GREEN / YELLOW / RED so the team only spends lawyer time on the ones that need it
- `$commercial-legal-renewal-tracker` — Show contracts with cancel-by deadlines coming up and warn before notice windows close, working from a maintained renewal register
- `$commercial-legal-review` — Review a vendor agreement, NDA, or SaaS subscription against your playbook
- `$commercial-legal-review-proposals` — Review and approve (or reject) pending playbook update proposals from the playbook-monitor agent and apply approved changes to the practice profile
- `$commercial-legal-saas-msa-review` — Reference: review of SaaS subscription agreements with attention to the terms that matter most in subscription deals — auto-renewal mechanics, price escalation,
- `$commercial-legal-stakeholder-summary` — Translates a contract review into a summary the business stakeholder will actually read
- `$commercial-legal-vendor-agreement-review` — Reference: review of an inbound vendor agreement against the team playbook in `${LEGAL_CONSULTANT_HOME:-~/.legal-consultant}/commercial-legal/CLAUDE.md`
- `$corporate-legal-ai-tool-handoff` — Detects when Luminance, Kira, or a similar bulk-review tool is in use, hands off the high-volume clause extraction to it, and QAs its output per the trust level
- `$corporate-legal-board-minutes` — Drafts board or committee meeting minutes in your house format
- `$corporate-legal-closing-checklist` — What's blocking close — maintain the closing checklist with status, critical path, and days to close
- `$corporate-legal-cold-start-interview` — House cold-start interview (jurisdiction, request list + prior memo), or --new-deal for deal-specific context
- `$corporate-legal-customize` — Guided customization of your corporate practice profile — change one thing without re-running the whole cold-start interview
- `$corporate-legal-deal-team-summary` — Aggregate diligence findings into a deal team briefing at the right altitude for the audience — exec summary for leadership, working summary for the team
- `$corporate-legal-diligence-issue-extraction` — Read VDR documents and extract issues per house categories and materiality thresholds, producing findings in house memo format
