| `social-insurance-law.md` | Social Insurance Law — نظام التأمينات الاجتماعية | Royal Decree No. M/273 of 26/12/1445H (2 July 2024), approving Council of Ministers Decision No. 1022 of 26/12/1445H. The Royal Decree and the Council decision each carry the transitional clauses (Second to Eleventh) that set the contribution phase-in, the retirement-age table, and which law applies to whom. Legacy law: Royal Decree No. M/33 of 3/9/1421H (29 November 2000), Council of Ministers Decision No. 199 of 17/8/1421H | 2024-07-03 (Art. 63: "يعمل به من اليوم التالي لتاريخ صدوره"; issued 2 July 2024; published in Umm al-Qura 29/12/1445H = 5 July 2024). The portal shows issue date 1445/12/26 and publication date 1445/12/29. Application "to new entrants only" is not in the law itself: it follows from Decree clause Second, which excludes (1) contributors with uncompensated contribution periods under the Civil Retirement Law or the 1421H law before 3 July 2024 and (2) existing pensioners; clause Fourth keeps the 1421H law, the Civil Retirement Law (M/41 of 1393H) and the Unemployment Insurance Law (M/18 of 1435H) in force for those two groups. Legacy law: issued 29 November 2000, published 12 January 2001 | 2026-09-04 (both laws, Arabic) | 27 | 27 | 0 | New law: https://laws.boe.gov.sa/BoeLaws/Laws/LawDetails/eaee8a20-3a54-4aaf-b0d9-b1ad00998962/1 . Legacy 1421H law: https://laws.boe.gov.sa/BoeLaws/Laws/LawDetails/8ff3cd90-e466-4bf9-a071-a9a700f2a70d/1 |
| `trade-names-law.md` | Trade Names Law — نظام الأسماء التجارية | Royal Decree No. M/83 of 19/3/1446H (22 September 2024), item Second, approving Council of Ministers Resolution No. 237 of 14/3/1446H. The task brief cited "M/84"; the portal page for this Law reproduces Royal Decree M/83, which approves the Commercial Register Law (item First) and the Trade Names Law (item Second) together. There is no M/84 for this Law | 2025-04-03 (Art. 23: "after 180 days from publication in the Official Gazette"; published 1/4/1446H = 4 October 2024; day 180 is 2 April 2025, so "after 180 days" gives 3 April 2025; the Ministry's announced go-live of 3 April 2025 is `[model knowledge — verify]`) | 2026-09-04 | 13 | 13 | 0 | [link](https://laws.boe.gov.sa/BoeLaws/Laws/LawDetails/d4801a45-7f76-4414-bdca-b20900db6fc4/1) |
| `ultimate-beneficial-ownership-rules.md` | Ultimate Beneficial Owner Rules — قواعد المستفيد الحقيقي | Per the Ministry of Commerce guidance document read today: Minister of Commerce Decision No. (99) dated 5/6/1447H (`[authority — MoC]`). The amendment-watch lead 2.4 (law-firm notes, unconfirmed) cites "Ministerial Decision No. 267 dated 26 Nov 2025"; 5/6/1447H falls on or about 26 November 2025, so the two references are probably the same decision and the number (99 versus 267) is an unresolved discrepancy `[model knowledge — verify]` | Not printed in the guidance document. Lead 2.4 claims 2026-01-04 `[model knowledge — verify]`. The guide's worked example (company incorporated 08/12/2025 that disclosed its UBO with the incorporation application, annual confirmation due 07/12/2026) is consistent with the Rules operating from late 2025 or early 2026 | 2026-09-04 (the MoC guide, in full; Companies Law Arts. 262, 264, and 274 in Arabic from `boe/companies-law-1443-ar.md`). Rows below tagged `[authority — MoC]` were read from the guide, which paraphrases the Rules and cites their article numbers; the Rules' own wording was not read | 16 | 13 | 3 | Ministry of Commerce guidance document: الدليل الإرشادي للمستفيد الحقيقي، النسخة رقم (2) 2025م ("UBO Guidance Manual, Version 2, 2025"), fetched from mc.gov.sa as `authority/moc-bog.txt` (page URL not captured in the fetch; the MoC news item at https://mc.gov.sa/en/mediacenter/News/Pages/09-12-25-01.aspx is the lead's pointer). The text of the Rules themselves (the ministerial decision) was not in the source set |

