| Arts. 40, 96 | In an adhesion contract acceptance is mere submission to fixed terms the offeror does not allow to be negotiated. If an adhesion contract contains abusive (ta'assufi) terms the court may amend them or relieve the adhering party of them as justice requires; any contrary agreement is void. | إذا تمَّ العقد بطريق الإذعان وتضمن شروطًا تعسفيةً؛ فللمحكمة أن تعدلها أو تعفي الطرف المـُذْعِن منها وفقًا لما تقتضيه العدالة. ويقع باطلًا كل اتفاق على خلاف ذلك. | Non-negotiable SaaS terms of service and standard vendor terms are adhesion contracts on the Art. 40 definition. A Saudi customer can ask a court to rewrite abusive terms (broad exclusions, unilateral price changes) and the clause cannot opt out. Whether courts will apply this to B2B contracts between sophisticated parties, given the Decree para. 6 "nature of commercial transaction" carve-out, is unsettled `[model knowledge — verify]`. Ambiguities are also read against the drafter (Art. 104(3)). | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 41 | Negotiating a contract creates no duty to conclude it, but a party who negotiates or breaks off negotiations in bad faith is liable for the other party's loss, excluding expected profit from the contract. Bad faith includes lack of seriousness and deliberate failure to disclose a material fact affecting the contract. | يكون من يتفاوض أو يُنهي التفاوض بسوء نية مسؤولًا عن الضرر الذي أصاب الطرف الآخر، ولا يشمل ذلك التَّعويض عمَّا فاته من كسب متوقع … يُعدُّ من سوء النية عدم الجدية في التفاوض، أو تعمد عدم الإدلاء ببيانٍ جوهريٍّ مؤثرٍ في العقد. | Term sheets and LOIs marked non-binding are non-binding, but walking away to use a competing bid, or concealing a material fact during RFP responses, exposes the party to reliance damages. Non-binding LOIs should still state the parties' freedom to withdraw. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 42-44 | Agreement on the essential matters with deferral of non-essential ones is a concluded contract; the court fixes unresolved non-essential terms by law, nature of the transaction and custom, unless the parties tied formation to later agreement. A promise to contract binds only if the essential terms and the period for concluding are fixed and the formalities of the intended contract are met; a judgment then stands in place of the contract. Payment of earnest money (arboun) on contracting means the payer alone may withdraw from the contract, forfeiting the arboun; if no withdrawal period is fixed the court sets it by custom; silence or non-performance within the period is withdrawal. All subject to contrary agreement. | إذا اتفق المتعاقدان على المسائل الجوهرية في العقد وعلى إرجاء الاتفاق على المسائل غير الجوهرية؛ كان ذلك كافيًا لاعتبار القبول مطابقًا للإيجاب … لا يكون الوعد … ملزمًا إلا إذا عُيّنت المسائل الجوهرية في العقد المراد إبرامه، والمدة التي يجب إبرامه فيها. … دفع العربون عند إبرام العقد يفيد أن لدافع العربون وحده الحق في العدول عن العقد، وليس له إذا عدل أن يسترد مبلغ العربون، وذلك كله ما لم يتفق على خلافه. | "Subject to contract" language matters: without it, an agreed scope and price with open boilerplate is a binding contract. Options and rights of first refusal need essential terms and a deadline to be enforceable as promises to contract. A "deposit" paid at signing is by default an option fee giving the payer a walk-away right. If a deposit is meant as part-payment with no withdrawal right, say so expressly. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 45-46 | A framework agreement fixes the basic terms governing contracts the parties later conclude under it and forms part of those contracts. Express or implied reference to a standard document, rules or any other document makes it part of the contract. | الاتفاق الإطاري عقدٌ يُحدد المتعاقدان بمقتضاه البنود الأساسية التي تخضع لها العقود التي ينشئها المتعاقدان بينهما … إذا أحال المتعاقدان صراحةً أو ضمنًا في العقد إلى أحكام وثيقةٍ نموذجيَّةٍ أو قواعد محددة أو أي وثيقة أخرى عُدَّت جزءًا من العقد. | MSA + order-form structures are expressly recognised. Incorporation by reference (URLs to online terms, SLAs, AUPs, DPAs) works, including implied reference; the reviewer should still capture the referenced version because the referenced document is part of the contract. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 57-67 (mistake, fraud, duress) | A party may seek annulment for a fundamental mistake without which it would not have contracted (as to the object's quality, the other party's identity or attributes, or the legal rule), but only if the other party shared, knew of, or could easily have detected the mistake. A mere clerical or arithmetical error does not affect the contract. A mistaken party may not rely on the mistake contrary to good faith and is bound by the contract it intended if the other party offers to perform it. Fraud (taghrir) is deceiving the other party by fraudulent means into a contract it would not otherwise have made; deliberate silence to conceal a matter the other party would not have contracted knowing of it is fraud. The victim may seek annulment if the fraud concerned a fundamental matter. Third-party fraud allows annulment only if the contracting party knew or ought to have known of it. Duress is an unlawful threat, physical or moral, that frightens a person into acting; it requires a threat of serious imminent harm to the person, honour or property of the coerced or another, without which the contract would not have been made; the coerced party may seek annulment if the duress came from the other party, or from a third party the other party knew or should have known of. | للمتعاقد طلب إبطال العقد إذا وقع في غلط جوهري لولاه لم يرض بالعقد … لا يُعتد بغلط المتعاقد إلا إذا كان المتعاقد الآخر قد وقع معه في الغلط نفسه أو علم بوقوعه فيه أو كان من السهل عليه أن يتبينه. لا يؤثر في العقد مجرد الغلط المادي في الحساب أو الكتابة. … التغرير أن يخدع أحد المتعاقدين الآخر بطرق احتياليَّةٍ … يعد تغريرًا تعمد السكوت لإخفاء أمرٍ لم يكن المغرر به ليبرم العقد لو علم به. … الإكراه تهديد شخصٍ دون حقٍّ بوسيلةٍ ماديَّةٍ أو معنويَّةٍ تُخيفه فتحمله على التصرف … للمُكرَه طلب إبطال العقد إذا صدر الإكراه من المتعاقد الآخر. | Pricing typos in an order form are corrected, not a ground to escape the deal. "Mistake as to the legal rule" is expressly a ground, which is unusual and gives a party who misunderstood a regulatory constraint an argument. Non-disclosure is actionable fraud, so "no reliance on representations outside this agreement" clauses do not protect a party that deliberately concealed a material fact. Read with Art. 173 (no exclusion of liability for ghish). Commercial pressure (threat to exercise a lawful termination right) is not "without right" and is not duress. Threats to withhold performance already owed could be. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 68-69 | Where a party exploits the other's manifest weakness or pressing need to obtain a contract causing it gross unfairness (ghabn), the court may on the victim's application reduce its obligations, increase the other's, or annul the contract; the action must be brought within 180 days of contracting. Ghabn is an excess or shortfall in the consideration beyond what is customary, determined by custom; ghabn alone does not permit annulment except for incapacitated persons' property or where statute so provides, and never in auctions; the other party may avert annulment by offering what the court considers sufficient to remove the ghabn. | إذا استغل أحد المتعاقدين ضعفًا ظاهرًا أو حاجة ملحة في المتعاقد الآخر، لإبرام عقدٍ لحقه منه غبنٌ، فللمحكمة … أن تنقص من التزاماته أو تزيد من التزامات المتعاقد الآخر أو تبطل العقد، ويجب أن ترفع الدعوى بذلك خلال (مائة وثمانين) يومًا من تاريخ التعاقد. | An unfavourable price by itself is not a ground to reopen a B2B contract; exploitation of a pressing need (e.g. an emergency supply at an extortionate price) is, but the 180-day (Hijri) window is short. Diligence: check whether any contract signed under distress is within the window. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 72, 74-76 | The object must be possible, not contrary to public order, and determined or determinable, or the contract is void. The contract may contain any term the parties agree that meets those conditions; a void term is severed alone, but a party may seek annulment of the whole contract if it would not have contracted without the term. A contract whose motivating cause is unlawful, if expressed or apparent from circumstances, is void; an unstated cause is presumed lawful. | يجوز أن يتضمن العقد أي شرطٍ يرتضيه المتعاقدان إذا توفرت فيه الشروط … إذا تضمن العقد شرطًا باطلًا بطل الشرط وحده، وللمتعاقد طلب إبطال العقد إذا تبيّن أنه ما كان ليرضى بالعقد دون ذلك الشرط. | Freedom of contract is the rule; "public order" (النظام العام) is the limit and is undefined. In practice Sharia prohibitions (riba, gharar/excessive uncertainty, gambling) are treated as public order `[model knowledge — verify]`. Severability clauses restate the statutory default; they cannot remove the party's right to annul if the void term was essential. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 79, 81, 84 | An annulment action is not heard after 1 year from knowledge of the ground (for incapacity or duress, 1 year from capacity being complete or duress ceasing) and in any event after 10 years from contracting (except incapacity). Nullity (butlan) may be invoked by any interested person and raised by the court of its own motion, cannot be cured by ratification, and the action is barred after 10 years from contracting but nullity may be pleaded as a defence at any time. Partial nullity or voidability affects only that part unless the party would not have contracted without it. | لا تسمع دعوى إبطال العقد إذا انقضت (سنة) من تاريخ العلم بسبب الإبطال … لا تسمع دعوى البطلان إذا انقضت (عشر) سنوات من تاريخ التعاقد، ولكن لكل ذي مصلحة أن يدفع ببطلان العقد في أي وقت. إذا كان العقد في جزء منه باطلًا أو يجوز إبطاله؛ يبطل ذلك الجزء فقط. | Voidable (mistake, fraud, duress) claims go stale fast: 1 Hijri year from discovery. Void (unlawful object/cause) contracts can be attacked for 10 years and defended against indefinitely. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 94 | A validly concluded contract may not be revoked or amended except by agreement or by statute. Rights created by the contract vest on conclusion without depending on delivery unless statute provides otherwise, and the parties must perform what the contract imposes. | إذا تم العقد صحيحًا لم يجز نقضه أو تعديله إلا بالاتفاق أو بمقتضى نص نظامي. تثبت الحقوق التي يُنشئها العقد فور انعقاده … ويجب على المتعاقدين الوفاء بما أوجبه العقد عليهما. | Pacta sunt servanda in statutory form. Unilateral vendor rights to change terms, prices or SLAs are enforceable only because the contract itself grants them (the "by agreement" limb); the reviewer should treat a unilateral-modification clause as a negotiated concession, and note the Art. 96 adhesion-contract risk if the clause is abusive. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 95 | A contract must be performed according to its contents and in a manner consistent with good faith. It binds the party not only to what it states but to what follows from it under statute, custom and the nature of the contract. | يجب تنفيذ العقد طبقًا لما اشتمل عليه وبطريقة تتفق مع ما يوجبه حسن النية. لا يقتصر العقد على إلزام المتعاقد بما ورد فيه، ولكن يشمل ما هو من مستلزماته وفقًا لما تقضي به النصوص النظامية والعرف وطبيعة العقد. | Implied terms exist by statute. An "entire agreement" clause does not exclude terms implied by custom and the nature of the contract; a cooperation duty and a duty not to frustrate the other party's performance will be implied. Good faith is a performance standard, not a free-standing cause of action for pre-contract conduct (that is Art. 41). | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 97 | Hardship: where general exceptional circumstances that could not be foreseen at contracting make performance onerous for the debtor so as to threaten it with a grave loss, the debtor may without undue delay invite the other party to negotiate; the request does not entitle the debtor to withhold performance; if no agreement is reached within a reasonable period the court may, weighing both parties' interests, reduce the onerous obligation to a reasonable level. Any agreement contrary to this article is void. | إذا طرأت ظروف استثنائيةٌ عامَّةٌ لم يكن في الوسع توقعها وقت التعاقد وترتب على حدوثها أن يصير تنفيذ الالتزام التعاقدي مرهقًا للمدين بحيث يهدده بخسارةٍ فادحةٍ؛ فله -دون تأخرٍ غير مسوغ- دعوة الطرف الآخر للتفاوض. طلب التفاوض لا يخول المدين الامتناع عن تنفيذ الالتزام. إذا لم يُتوصل إلى اتِّفاقٍ خلال مدَّةٍ معقولةٍ؛ فللمحكمة تبعًا للظروف وبعد الموازنة بين مصلحة الطرفين أن ترد الالتزام المرهق إلى الحد المعقول. يقع باطلًا كل اتفاق على خلاف أحكام هذه المادة. | Mandatory: a clause saying "no adjustment for change in circumstances", or a fixed-price clause purporting to exclude judicial rebalancing, is void to that extent. The trigger is narrow (general, unforeseeable, threatening a grave loss, not mere loss of profit), the debtor must keep performing, and negotiation is a precondition. A well-drafted change-in-law / price-adjustment clause is the practical way to control the outcome, since the court "reduces" the obligation rather than terminating. For muqawala there is a specific rebalancing article (Art. 471(3)). | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 98-99 | The contract's effect extends to the parties and their universal successors (subject to inheritance rules) unless the contract, the nature of the transaction or statute shows otherwise; personal rights and obligations attached to a thing pass to a particular successor with the thing if they are among its requisites and the successor knew of them. A contract imposes no obligation on third parties but may confer a right on them. | ينصرف أثر العقد إلى المتعاقدين والخلف العام … لا يرتب العقد التزامًا في ذمة الغير، ولكن يجوز أن يكسبه حقًّا. | A share sale (change of control) does not by itself transfer or terminate contracts: the company remains the party. An asset sale does not carry contracts over without the counterparty's consent (Art. 255), except obligations that are "requisites" of the transferred asset and known to the buyer. Change-of-control clauses are therefore a matter of drafting, not statute. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 101-102 | A person may stipulate in its own name for the benefit of a third party if it has a material or moral interest; the beneficiary acquires a direct right against the promisor (unless agreed otherwise), and the promisor may raise defences arising from the contract. The stipulator (not its creditors or heirs) may revoke or substitute the beneficiary unless the beneficiary has notified acceptance or revocation would harm the promisor. | يترتب على الاشتراط لمصلحة الغير أن يَكسِبَ الغير حقًّا مباشرًا تجاه المتعهد يستطيع أن يطالبه بوفائه ما لم يُتفق على خلاف ذلك. | Affiliate beneficiary clauses (customer affiliates may enforce the MSA) and third-party indemnitee provisions are enforceable. A "no third-party beneficiaries" clause is the contrary agreement the article contemplates. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 104 | If the wording of the contract is clear, it is not departed from on the pretext of interpreting it to find the parties' intention. Where interpretation is needed, the common intention is sought beyond the literal meaning, guided by custom, the circumstances, the nature of the transaction, the parties' course of dealing and the honesty and trust that should prevail; terms are construed together. Doubt is construed in favour of the party bearing the obligation or condition, and in adhesion contracts in favour of the adhering party. | إذا كانت عبارة العقد واضحةً فلا يُعدل عن مدلولها بحجة تفسيرها بحثًا عن إرادة المتعاقدين … يُفسر الشك لمصلحة من يتحمل عبء الالتزام أو الشرط، ويُفسر في عقود الإذعان لمصلحة الطرف المـُذْعِن. | Precision in drafting is rewarded: a clear exclusion, cap or termination trigger will be applied as written. Ambiguity cuts against the obligee (the party seeking to enforce) and against the drafter of standard terms. An Arabic/English "prevailing language" clause is respected as part of the clear wording; without one, the court will read the Arabic version `[model knowledge — verify]`. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 105-106 | The parties may mutually rescind (iqala) the contract in whole or part on the contract's terms. A contract may be concluded with an option to withdraw (khiyar al-shart): the option holder may withdraw within the fixed period on notice to the other party, which counts as termination; if no period is fixed the court sets it by custom; the option lapses by express or implied waiver or expiry of the period. | يجوز التعاقد بشرط الخيار في العدول عن العقد، ولمن له الخيار حق العدول خلال المدة المعينة بشرط إعلام المتعاقد الآخر، فإذا عدل من له الخيار عُدَّ ذلك فسخًا للعقد. | Termination-for-convenience rights and trial/cooling-off periods are statutorily recognised options and need no cause; give them a defined period and a notice mechanism or the court will fix the period. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 107 | In bilateral contracts, if a party does not perform, the other may, after serving notice (i'thar) on the defaulting party, demand performance or termination, with compensation in either case where warranted; the court may refuse termination if the unperformed part is of little importance relative to the obligation. | في العقود الملزمة للجانبين، إذا لم يوف أحد المتعاقدين بالتزامه، فللمتعاقد الآخر بعد إعذاره المتعاقد المخل أن يطلب تنفيذ العقد أو فسخه، مع التعويض في الحالتين إن كان له مقتض، وللمحكمة أن ترفض طلب الفسخ إذا كان الجزء الذي لم يوف به المخل قليل الأهمية بالنسبة إلى الالتزام. | Default termination is judicial: without a termination clause, the innocent party must serve notice and then ask the court. There is no statutory materiality threshold beyond "little importance", so the contract should define material breach and cure periods. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 108 | The parties may agree that the creditor may terminate the contract on the debtor's breach without a court judgment; such agreement does not dispense with the notice (i'thar) unless the parties expressly agree to dispense with it. | يجوز الاتفاق على أن يكون للدائن حق فسخ العقد عند إخلال المدين بالتزاماته دون حاجة إلى حكم قضائي، ولا يُعفي هذا الاتفاق من الإعذار إلا إذا اتفق المتعاقدان صراحةً على الإعفاء منه. | Contractual termination clauses work, but a termination "immediately on breach without notice" is effective only if the clause expressly waives i'thar. Draft: "without need for a court order or any notice, formal demand or i'thar". A cure-period notice satisfies i'thar (Art. 177). | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 109 | Contracts of exchange are deemed concluded on the basis that the object is free of defects, except those custom tolerates; a defect custom does not tolerate is a breach of obligation. | تُعدُّ عقود المعاوضات منعقدةً على أساس سلامة محل العقد من العيوب إلا ما جرى العرف على التسامح فيه. | A statutory implied quality warranty applies to services and software as well as goods. "AS IS" disclaimers work only within the limits of Arts. 173 and 343 (no exclusion for fraud/gross fault or deliberately concealed defects). | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 110, 174, 292-294 (impossibility, force majeure risk, release) | In bilateral contracts, if performance becomes impossible for a cause not attributable to the debtor, its obligation and the counter-obligation are extinguished and the contract is dissolved automatically. Partial or temporary impossibility (in continuing contracts) extinguishes only the affected part; the creditor may seek termination, which the court may refuse if the impossible part is of little importance. The parties may agree that the debtor bears the risk of force majeure. Release (ibra') by the creditor extinguishes the obligation without the debtor's acceptance, though the debtor may reject it; release is valid only of an existing debt, even if not yet due; it is subject to the substantive rules on gifts and needs no particular form. An obligation is extinguished if the debtor proves performance became impossible for a cause beyond its control, and the counter-obligation with it. | إذا أصبح تنفيذ الالتزام مستحيلًا بسببٍ لا يد للمدين فيه، انقضى التزامه والالتزام المقابل له، وانفسخ العقد من تلقاء نفسه. … يجوز الاتفاق على أن يتحمل المدين تبعة القوة القاهرة. … ينقضي التزام المدين إذا أبرأه الدائن، ولا يتوقف الإبراء على قبول المدين … ينقضي التزام المدين إذا أثبت استحالة التنفيذ عليه بسبب لا يد له فيه. | Statutory force majeure effect: automatic dissolution on total impossibility, suspension on temporary impossibility. The threshold is impossibility, not impracticability (that is Art. 97 hardship). A force majeure clause is therefore mainly useful to (a) define events, (b) add notice/mitigation duties, (c) fix suspension and long-stop termination mechanics, and (d) allocate the risk (Art. 174). Force majeure protection is a default, not mandatory: a clause excluding force majeure relief for the vendor (or for specified events such as subcontractor failure or pandemics) is enforceable. Compare Art. 97 hardship, which cannot be contracted out of. Waivers and releases in settlement agreements need no form. Releases of future claims are not "existing debts" and are exposed to challenge; settle specific existing claims. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 111-112 | On termination or dissolution the parties are restored to their pre-contract position; if impossible, the court may award compensation. For continuing (time) contracts termination has no retroactive effect, and the court may award compensation. Termination is not opposable to a good-faith particular successor who acquired a real right. | إذا كان العقد من العقود الزمنية فلا يكون للفسخ أو الانفساخ أثرٌ رجعيٌّ. | Subscriptions, licences and service agreements are continuing contracts: termination is prospective, so fees for periods already served are not refundable by operation of law; refund of prepaid unused fees is a drafting point. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 113 | Termination of the contract does not extinguish a dispute-resolution clause or a confidentiality clause, unless agreed otherwise, without prejudice to other laws. | دون إخلال بالنصوص النظامية، لا يزول بفسخ العقد شرط الالتزام بتسوية المنازعة ولا شرط الالتزام بالسرية؛ ما لم يتفق على خلاف ذلك. | Confidentiality and arbitration/jurisdiction clauses survive termination by statute. Other survival items (limitation of liability, indemnities, non-solicit, audit rights) survive only if the survival clause says so; the reviewer should still check the survival clause lists them. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 114, 191 | In bilateral contracts where mutual obligations are due, either party may withhold its performance while the other withholds its own. More generally, anyone bound to render something may withhold it while the creditor has not performed a connected obligation arising from the debtor's obligation and has not given adequate security. | إذا كانت الالتزامات المتقابلة مستحقة الوفاء جاز لأي من المتعاقدين أن يمتنع عن تنفيذ التزامه ما دام المتعاقد الآخر ممتنعًا عن تنفيذ ما التزم به. | Statutory suspension right: a vendor may suspend services for non-payment of due fees without a suspension clause, and a customer may withhold payment for undelivered milestones. Contractual "no set-off, pay first, dispute later" clauses contract out of this; note Art. 96 if the contract is one of adhesion. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 120, 125, 127-129, 143 | Every fault that causes harm to another obliges its author to compensate. A person is not liable if the harm arose from a cause beyond its control such as force majeure, a third party's fault or the victim's fault, unless agreed otherwise. Multiple tortfeasors are jointly and severally liable; the court apportions and, failing that, shares equally. A victim whose fault contributed to or increased the harm loses its right in proportion. A principal (matbu') is liable to the victim for harm caused by its subordinate's fault in or because of the work, where it had actual authority to supervise and direct, with recourse against the subordinate. A tort compensation action is not heard after 3 years from the victim's knowledge of the harm and of the person responsible, and in any event after 10 years from the harm; where the claim arises from a crime it remains admissible while the criminal action is. | كل خطأٍ سبب ضررًا للغير يُلزم من ارتكبه بالتعويض … لا يكون الشخص مسؤولًا إذا ثبت أن الضرر قد نشأ عن سببٍ لا يد له فيه، كقوةٍ قاهرةٍ أو خطأ الغير أو خطأ المتضرر؛ ما لم يُتفق على خلاف ذلك. … إذا تعدد المسؤولون عن فعل ضار كانوا متضامنين في التزامهم بتعويض الضرر … يكون المتبوع مسؤولًا تجاه المتضرر عن الضرر الذي يحدثه تابعه بخطئه أثناء تأدية عمله أو بسبب هذا العمل. … لا تُسمع دعوى التعويض الناشئة عن الفعل الضار بانقضاء (ثلاث) سنوات من تاريخ علم المتضرر بوقوع الضرر وبالمسؤول عنه. وفي جميع الأحوال لا تسمع الدعوى بانقضاء (عشر) سنوات من تاريخ وقوع الضرر. | General fault-based tort. Contract counterparties can sue in tort where the contract does not cover the loss; Art. 173(2) prevents excluding tort liability by agreement, which is why Saudi limitation-of-liability clauses do not reliably cap tort claims `[model knowledge — verify]`. Vicarious liability for employees and directed contractors. Indemnities for "acts of personnel" restate the statutory position; the important drafting point is the contractual allocation between the parties, since joint liability towards the victim cannot be excluded (Art. 173(2)). Tort claims have a shorter window than contract claims (10 years, Art. 295). | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 136-138 | Compensation must repair the harm in full, restoring the victim to the position it was or could have been in but for the harm. Recoverable harm is the loss suffered and the profit lost, if a natural result of the harmful act; harm is a natural result if the victim could not have avoided it by the reasonable effort of an ordinary person. Compensation for a harmful act includes moral damage (physical or psychological suffering of a natural person from injury to body, liberty, honour, reputation or social standing); the court assesses it. | يتحدد الضرر الذي يلتزم المسؤول بالتعويض عنه بقدر ما لحق المتضرر من خسارةٍ وما فاته من كسب، إذا كان ذلك نتيجةً طبيعيةً للفعل الضار. ويعد كذلك إذا لم يكن في مقدور المتضرر تفاديه ببذل الجهد المعقول … يشمل التعويضُ عن الفعل الضار التعويضَ عن الضرر المعنوي. | Lost profit is recoverable by statute (a change from prior Saudi practice, which was restrictive `[model knowledge — verify]`). Mitigation is built into causation. Moral damages are defined for natural persons only; a company's reputational loss must be pleaded as material loss. These articles are imported into contract damages by Art. 180. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 161, 164, 167-169 | The debtor must perform when due; if it refuses, performance is compelled where the statutory conditions for enforcement are met. After notice, the debtor is compelled to specific performance where possible; if specific performance would be oppressive to the debtor the court may, on its application, confine the creditor to compensation if that causes the creditor no serious harm. For an obligation to do: the creditor may refuse performance by a third party where the contract or the nature of the work requires personal performance; if the debtor fails, the creditor may with court permission (or without it in urgency) have the obligation performed at the debtor's expense. For an obligation to preserve, manage or exercise care, the debtor performs by exercising the care of an ordinary person even if the purpose is not achieved, unless statute provides otherwise; where the obligation is to achieve a result, performance occurs only when the result is achieved. Breach of an obligation not to do entitles the creditor to removal of the breach at the debtor's expense plus compensation. | يُجبَر المدين بعد إعذاره على تنفيذ التزامه تنفيذًا عينيًّا متى كان ذلك ممكنًا. إذا كان في التنفيذ العيني إرهاقٌ للمدين جاز للمحكمة بناءً على طلبه أن تقصر حق الدائن على اقتضاء التعويض. … إذا كان المطلوب من المدين هو المحافظة على الشيء أو القيام بإدارته أو توخي الحيطة في تنفيذ التزامه، فإنه يكون قد وفى بالالتزام إذا بذل في تنفيذه عناية الشخص المعتاد ولو لم يتحقق الغرض المقصود … أما إذا كان المطلوب هو تحقيق غاية فلا يُعدُّ الوفاء حاصلًا إلا بتحقق تلك الغاية. | Specific performance is the primary remedy, not an exceptional one; injunction-style relief to compel a vendor to continue services or deliver is available in principle. Clauses stating that damages are the sole remedy are enforceable as agreements under Art. 94 but sit uneasily with this default `[model knowledge — verify]`. The means/result distinction is statutory: "reasonable efforts" and "shall achieve" language will be given effect literally. Step-in / replacement-vendor rights exist by default (court permission needed unless urgent); a contractual step-in clause removes the need for permission. Non-compete and non-solicit covenants are obligations not to do, enforceable by removal plus damages subject to public order and the Labor Law for employees `[model knowledge — verify]`. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 170-172 | The debtor is ordered to pay compensation for non-performance where specific performance is impossible, including where the debtor's delay makes performance useless to the creditor; on delay the creditor may set a reasonable period and then claim compensation for non-performance; no compensation is due if the debtor proves the failure was due to a cause beyond its control. Delay itself obliges the debtor to compensate the creditor's loss from the delay unless caused by a cause beyond its control. The creditor's contributory fault reduces compensation per Art. 128. | إذا تأخر المدين في تنفيذ التزامه وجب عليه تعويض الدائن عما يلحقه من ضرر بسبب التأخير، ما لم يثبت أن تأخير الوفاء بسبب لا يد له فيه. | Delay damages are the statutory vehicle for late payment and late delivery. The Law has no article awarding interest on money debts; compensation for late payment must be proved as actual loss, and any fixed percentage running with time risks characterisation as riba, which is prohibited under Sharia as applied in the Kingdom and treated as public order `[model knowledge — verify]`. See Arts. 178 (no pre-agreed compensation for money obligations) and 385 (loan increase void). | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 173 | The parties may agree to exempt the debtor from compensation for harm arising from non-performance or delay in performing its contractual obligation, except harm arising from the debtor's fraud (ghish) or gross fault. Liability arising from a harmful act (tort) may not be excluded by agreement. | يجوز الاتفاق على إعفاء المدين من التعويض عن الضرر الناشئ عن عدم تنفيذ التزامه التعاقدي أو تأخره فيه، إلا ما يكون عن غش أو خطأ جسيم منه. لا يجوز الاتفاق على الإعفاء من المسؤولية المترتبة على الفعل الضار. | Exclusion and limitation clauses (caps, consequential-loss exclusions) are valid for contractual liability, but never for fraud or gross fault, and never for tort. Every cap should carve out fraud and gross negligence expressly to match the statute; a cap that purports to cover "any liability howsoever arising" is partly void. "Gross fault" (خطأ جسيم) is undefined; expect it to be argued for reckless or wilful default `[model knowledge — verify]`. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Arts. 175-177 | Compensation is due only after notice (i'thar) to the debtor unless agreed or provided otherwise. Notice is not required where the parties agreed expressly or impliedly that the debtor is in default on the due date, where performance became impossible or useless by the debtor's act, for tort compensation, for restitution of something received knowingly without right, or where the debtor declared in writing that it will not perform. Notice may be given by any agreed means or any statutory means of service, including filing suit. | لا يُستحق التعويض إلا بعد إعذار المدين؛ ما لم يوجد اتفاق أو نص نظامي بخلاف ذلك … يكون الإعذار بأي وسيلة متفق عليها بين المتعاقدين، أو بأي وسيلة مقررة نظامًا للتبليغ، بما في ذلك رفع الدعوى. | Damages and termination both hinge on i'thar. A notices clause fixing the means (email to a named address) is the "agreed means" and should be drafted with i'thar in mind. A "time is of the essence" or "default occurs automatically on the due date without notice" clause is the Art. 176(a) agreement. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 178 | The parties may fix the amount of compensation in advance in the contract or a later agreement, unless the object of the obligation is a sum of money; notice is not a condition of entitlement to such compensation. | يجوز للمتعاقدين أن يحددا مقدمًا مقدار التعويض بالنص عليه في العقد أو في اتفاقٍ لاحقٍ؛ ما لم يكن محل الالتزام مبلغًا نقديًّا، ولا يشترط لاستحقاق التعويض الإعذار. | Liquidated damages (delay LDs, service credits, penalty clauses) are valid for non-monetary obligations. They are not permitted for obligations to pay money: a late-payment charge fixed in advance (e.g. "2% per month on overdue invoices") is outside this article, so late-payment compensation must be proved as actual loss under Art. 171, and a fixed percentage running with time is exposed to the riba objection `[model knowledge — verify]`. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |
| Art. 179 | Agreed compensation is not due if the debtor proves the creditor suffered no harm. The court may, on the debtor's application, reduce agreed compensation if the debtor proves it was exaggerated or the principal obligation was partly performed. The court may, on the creditor's application, increase agreed compensation to the amount of the harm if the creditor proves the harm exceeded the agreed amount as a result of the debtor's fraud or gross fault. Any agreement contrary to this article is void. | لا يكون التعويض الاتفاقيُّ مستحَقًّا إذا أثبت المدين أن الدائن لم يلحقه أي ضرر. للمحكمة بناءً على طلب المدين أن تنقص هذا التعويض إذا أثبت أن التعويض المتفق عليه كان مبالغًا فيه أو أن الالتزام الأصلي قد نُفذ جزء منه. للمحكمة بناءً على طلب الدائن أن تزيد هذا التعويض إلى ما يساوي الضرر إذا أثبت أن الضرر جاوز مقدار التعويض الاتفاقي نتيجة غش أو خطأٍ جسيمٍ من المدين. يقع باطلًا كلُّ اتفاقٍ يُخالف أحكام هذه المادة. | The single most important row for contract review. There is no penalty/LD distinction: every agreed sum is reviewable. (1) An LD clause yields nothing if the debtor proves no harm, so "payable whether or not loss is suffered" and "the parties agree the amount is a genuine pre-estimate and not subject to reduction" are void. (2) The court can cut an excessive amount and pro-rate for partial performance; the burden is on the debtor. (3) The creditor can go above the agreed sum only for fraud/gross fault, so an LD clause otherwise operates as a cap on delay damages — this is what makes "sole and exclusive remedy for delay" language work for the payer. Service-credit regimes in SaaS agreements are agreed compensation and fall under this article. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] |

exec
/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/commercial-legal-escalation-flagger/SKILL.md' in /Users/basimkhoja/Projects/Legal Consultant
 succeeded in 0ms:
---
name: commercial-legal-escalation-flagger
description: "Route a contract issue to the right approver per the escalation matrix in `${LEGAL_CONSULTANT_HOME:-~/.legal-consultant}/commercial-legal/CLAUDE.md`, and draft the ask. Use when the user says 'who needs to approve this', 'escalate this', 'does this need GC sign-off', 'route this for approval', or when another skill finds an issue that exceeds the reviewer's authority."
argument-hint: "[describe the issue, or reference a review memo]"
