/bin/zsh -lc "rg -n '"'^'"\\| (Art\\. (6 |9|10|11|12|13|16|17|19|24|38)|Arts\\. (9|10)|Law Art\\. (40|51)|Law Arts\\. (38|40|49))' references/jurisdictions/ksa/commercial-courts-law.md references/jurisdictions/ksa/arbitration-law.md" in /Users/basimkhoja/Projects/Legal Consultant
 succeeded in 0ms:
references/jurisdictions/ksa/commercial-courts-law.md:34:| Arts. 9–12; Regs Arts. 71–83 | Valid service addresses include: the verified or chosen electronic address; residence; the address registered with the postal authority; the commercial-register address for that activity; the address stated in the case papers; **the address stated in the contract, for disputes arising from that contract**; and an address chosen by a foreigner in the Kingdom. A party may designate a lawyer's address. Change of the case-papers address must be notified within 48 hours or service there remains effective. Electronic service is by SMS to the verified mobile, verified/chosen e-mail, or notification through a government e-account; other addresses are served through a licensed postal provider. A person resident abroad may be served under these rules where the parties have so agreed, without prejudice to international conventions; the Regulations require that address to be recorded in a document between the parties, provide diplomatic-channel service where that fails, and treat the contract address as valid for five years from the contract unless agreed otherwise. Legal persons: service on the legal representative, a general partner, the manager, the legal department, or a branch manager for branch disputes; foreign companies with a branch or commercial representative: on that branch manager or representative. | يعد عنواناً للتبليغ ... العنوان المدون في العقد محل التعامل في المنازعات الناشئة عن ذلك العقد ... على الطرف حال تغييره العنوان ... أن يبلغ المحكمة خلال (ثمانٍ وأربعين) ساعة. / دون إخلال بالاتفاقيات الدولية، يجوز تبليغ من يكون محل إقامته خارج المملكة ... متى وجد اتفاق بين الأطراف على ذلك. / لا تسري أحكام الفقرة (1/و) من المادة التاسعة من النظام بعد انقضاء خمس سنوات من تاريخ العقد ما لم يتفق الأطراف على خلاف ذلك. | The notices clause of a contract is also the service clause for Saudi litigation: a stale address in the contract can carry valid service for five years. Foreign counterparties should be advised that agreeing to service at a contract address (including e-mail) enables service abroad without letters rogatory. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
references/jurisdictions/ksa/commercial-courts-law.md:35:| Art. 13; Regs Arts. 89–93 | The court may fine a party up to SAR 10,000 for breach of case procedure or hearing order (final). Case data, papers and documents of commercial cases are open to the public for a fee equal to the cost of the service; on application by an interested person the court may declare certain papers or documents confidential vis-à-vis persons other than the court, without prejudice to the publicity of hearings. The Regulations treat a document as confidential where a law or competent-authority decision so provides, where the parties' agreement makes it confidential, or where access would infringe a trade secret; confidentiality cannot be claimed if the parties previously agreed there is none; the court's decision on confidentiality is not subject to any objection. | للمحكمة عند إخلال أحد الأطراف ... أن تأمر بفرض غرامة لا تتجاوز عشرة آلاف ريال ... يتاح اطلاع العموم على بيانات الدعاوى التجارية وأوراقها ومستنداتها لقاء مقابل مالي ... ويجوز - بناءً على طلب ذي مصلحة - تقرير سرية بعض أوراق الدعوى التجارية أو مستنداتها لغير المحكمة. | Commercial-court filings are public by default. A contractual confidentiality clause is a recognised ground for a sealing order under the draft Regulations, so NDA and MSA confidentiality clauses should expressly cover litigation filings and require the party filing to seek confidentiality. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
references/jurisdictions/ksa/commercial-courts-law.md:37:| Art. 16 (marked amended on the portal); Regs Arts. 48–50 | The commercial court has jurisdiction over: (1) disputes between merchants arising from their original or ancillary commercial activities; (2) claims against a merchant in commercial-contract disputes where the principal claim exceeds SAR 100,000 in the text read today (the Supreme Judicial Council may raise this figure); (3) as amended by Royal Decree M/191 of 29/11/1444H, disputes arising from the partnership contracts (عقود المشاركة) provided for in the Civil Transactions Law (original text: disputes between partners in a mudaraba); (4) claims and violations under the Companies Law; (5) under the Bankruptcy Law; (6) under the intellectual-property laws; (7) under the other commercial laws; (8) claims and requests concerning judicial custodians, trustees, liquidators and appointed experts where linked to a case within its jurisdiction; (9) compensation claims for harm arising from a case previously heard by the court. The draft Regulations: item (2) requires a contractual relationship (Regs Art. 48) and, in Regs Art. 49, states the threshold as SAR 500,000; item (3) requires a written contract (Regs Art. 50, drafted against the original mudaraba wording). | تختص المحكمة بالنظر في الآتي: المنازعات التي تنشأ بين التجار بسبب أعمالهم التجارية الأصلية أو التبعية. الدعاوى المقامة على التاجر في منازعات العقود التجارية، متى كانت قيمة المطالبة الأصلية في الدعوى تزيد على مائة ألف ريال، وللمجلس عند الاقتضاء زيادة هذه القيمة. المنازعات التي تنشأ عن عقود المشاركة المنصوص عليها في نظام المعاملات المدنية (النص النافذ بموجب المرسوم الملكي رقم م/191 وتاريخ 29/11/1444هـ؛ النص الأصلي: منازعات الشركاء في شركة المضاربة). الدعاوى والمخالفات الناشئة عن تطبيق أحكام نظام الشركات ... نظام الإفلاس ... أنظمة الملكية الفكرية ... الأنظمة التجارية الأخرى ... | Merchant-to-merchant contract claims go to the commercial court regardless of value. A non-merchant's claim against a merchant on a commercial contract goes to the commercial court only above the threshold; the Law text in force says SAR 100,000 (the M/191 amendment touched only paragraph (3)) while the draft Regulations say SAR 500,000, so whether the Council has raised the figure must be confirmed before any routing advice. Partnership-contract disputes under the Civil Transactions Law (including mudaraba as one form) are now expressly commercial-court matters. Company-law claims (shareholder disputes, director liability) and bankruptcy matters are commercial-court matters; Regs Art. 8 measures the claim by the sums in the statement of claim excluding costs and fees, or by the value of the underlying obligation for non-monetary relief. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` (in-force text including the M/191 amendment to paragraph (3)); threshold conflict flagged; `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
references/jurisdictions/ksa/commercial-courts-law.md:38:| Art. 17; Regs Arts. 51–55 | Unless the parties agree otherwise in writing, territorial jurisdiction lies with the court of the defendant's place of residence; if none in the Kingdom, the claimant's; the claim may also be brought where the contract was concluded, performed or was to be performed. Company cases: the court of the company's head office (claims against the company, by the company against a partner, between partners, or against managers/board members); branch-contract disputes may be brought where the branch is. The plea of lack of territorial jurisdiction is lost once the party makes any request or defence, including at the case-preparation stage. | ما لم يتفق الطرفان كتابة على غير ذلك ... يكون الاختصاص المكاني للمحكمة التي يقع في نطاق اختصاصها مكان إقامة المدعى عليه ... ويجوز أن تقام الدعوى في المحكمة التي أبرم العقد أو نفذ أو كان واجب التنفيذ في نطاقها. / في الدعاوى المتعلقة بالشركات، يكون الاختصاص المكاني للمحكمة التي يقع في نطاق اختصاصها المقر الرئيس للشركة. | A written venue clause choosing a particular Saudi commercial court (e.g. Riyadh) is effective; venue is optional, not exclusive, absent agreement. Raise a venue objection in the very first submission. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
references/jurisdictions/ksa/commercial-courts-law.md:40:| Art. 19; Regs Arts. 116–121 | In the cases the Regulations specify, the claimant must notify the defendant in writing to perform the claimed right at least 15 days before filing. Before registration, and under court supervision, the parties may undertake conciliation/mediation, exchange of documents and memoranda, or a meeting to define claims, defences and evidence, documented as the Regulations provide. Draft Regulations: the notice is required in all cases within the court's jurisdiction except penalty cases under commercial laws, cases with an administrative body as party, small claims and urgent requests; it must state the parties, subject, claims and supporting document, with proof attached to the statement of claim (failing which the cure procedure of Art. 21 applies); proof of a prior attempt at amicable settlement, conciliation or mediation counts as the notice once the 15-day period has elapsed. | يجب في الدعاوى التي تحددها اللائحة أن يخطر المدعي المدعى عليه كتابة بأداء الحق المدعى به قبل (خمسة عشر) يوماً على الأقل من إقامة الدعوى. / يعد في حكم الإخطار تقديم ما يثبت اللجوء إلى التسوية الودية والمصالحة والوساطة قبل قيد الدعوى بشرط مضي المدة. | Send a formal demand (through a traceable channel) at least 15 days before filing; a contractual notice-of-breach step, if evidenced, does double duty. Pre-filing exchange under Art. 19(2) also interrupts the five-year non-hearing period (Regs Art. 63) and shortens small-claims timelines (Regs Art. 324). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
references/jurisdictions/ksa/commercial-courts-law.md:42:| Art. 24; Regs Arts. 58–67 | Absent a special text, claims within the court's jurisdiction are not heard after five years from the date the claimed right arose, unless the defendant acknowledges the right or the claimant shows an excuse the court accepts. Draft Regulations: rights arising before the Law run from its entry into force; the period cannot be varied by agreement; waiver of the plea is valid only after the period has run; the period starts when the debt falls due; "excuse" includes a material or moral impediment for its duration; a judicial claim (even before an incompetent court) or an Art. 19(2) pre-filing step interrupts the period; the plea belongs to the debtor and is not raised by the court of its own motion; it may be raised at any stage including on appeal; abandoned or annulled claims count towards the period; non-hearing of the principal claim extends to dependent claims such as against a guarantor. | فيما لم يرد به نص خاص، لا تسمع الدعاوى التي تختص بنظرها المحكمة بعد مضي (خمس) سنوات من تاريخ نشوء الحق المدعى به، ما لم يقر المدعى عليه بالحق أو يتقدم المدعي بعذر تقبله المحكمة. / لا يقبل الاتفاق على خلاف المدة المحددة نظاماً لسماع الدعوى. | Five years is the working limitation period for commercial claims in the commercial court; a contractual limitation clause (longer or shorter) is not effective under the draft Regulations. Diligence on receivables and claims older than five years should treat them as at risk. Cross-check the Civil Transactions Law's own non-hearing periods where that law applies. `[model knowledge — verify]` | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
references/jurisdictions/ksa/commercial-courts-law.md:47:| Art. 38 | Absent a special text in the commercial laws, the evidence chapter applies to cases within the court's jurisdiction; no particular form is required to prove an obligation unless the parties agree otherwise; the court may rely on evidentiary procedures conducted in a foreign state unless contrary to public order; where the parties agree specific evidence rules the court applies them, subject to public order; absent a special text, the burden of proof may be shifted by agreement. | لا يلزم لإثبات الالتزام شكل خاص، ما لم تتفق الأطراف على غير ذلك. للمحكمة أن تعتدّ بإجراءات الإثبات التي جرت في دولة أجنبية ما لم تخالف أحكام النظام العام. دون إخلال بالنظام العام، إذا اتفق الأطراف على قواعد محددة في الإثبات؛ فَتُعمِل المحكمة اتفاقَهم. فيما لم يرد فيه نص خاص، يجوز الاتفاق على نقل عبء الإثبات. | Contractual evidence clauses ("entire agreement", "records conclusive absent manifest error", burden-shifting warranties) are given effect in commercial-court litigation subject to public order. Foreign depositions or discovery outputs can be relied on. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` |
references/jurisdictions/ksa/commercial-courts-law.md:62:| Art. 93; Art. 96; Decree ¶2–¶4 | Where the Law is silent, the Law of Civil Procedure applies to cases within the court's jurisdiction insofar as compatible with the commercial nature of the case. The Law entered into force 60 days after publication and repeals conflicting provisions; commercial circuits in general courts serve regions without a commercial court, with appeal to the nearest commercial court; Art. 35 of the Law of Civil Procedure (the former commercial-jurisdiction rule) is repealed. | فيما لم يرد فيه نص خاص في النظام، تطبق أحكام نظام المرافعات الشرعية على الدعاوى التي تختص بنظرها المحكمة بما لا يخالف طبيعة الدعوى التجارية. / يعمل بالنظام بعد (ستين) يوماً من تاريخ نشره في الجريدة الرسمية. | Gaps (joinder, intervention, recusal, letters rogatory) are filled from the Law of Civil Procedure, which is not in this folder. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` |
references/jurisdictions/ksa/arbitration-law.md:53:| Law Arts. 49–50 (para. 1(b) as amended by Royal Decree M/21 of 26/1/1447H) | Awards under the Law are not subject to any appeal other than an annulment action. Annulment lies only where: (a) there is no arbitration agreement, or it is void, voidable or lapsed by expiry of its period; (b) a party to the agreement lacked capacity or had limited capacity when it was made, under the law governing its capacity (in-force wording: عديم الأهلية); (c) a party could not present its defence for want of proper notice of an arbitrator's appointment or of the proceedings, or for another reason beyond its control; (d) the award set aside the legal rules the parties agreed to apply to the merits; (e) the tribunal was constituted or the arbitrators appointed contrary to the Law or the parties' agreement; (f) the award decided matters outside the agreement (severable parts survive); (g) the award failed to meet the required conditions in a way affecting its content, or rests on void procedures that affected it. The court annuls of its own motion an award contrary to Sharia or public order in the Kingdom, or to the parties' agreement, or on a non-arbitrable subject. The arbitration agreement survives annulment unless agreed otherwise or the agreement itself is annulled; the court may not review the facts or merits. | لا تقبل دعوى بطلان حكم التحكيم إلا في الأحوال الآتية: ... ب- إذا كان أحد طرفي اتفاق التحكيم وقت إبرامه عديم الأهلية، أو ناقصها، وفقاً للنظام الذي يحكم أهليته (النص النافذ بموجب المرسوم الملكي رقم م/21 وتاريخ 26/1/1447هـ) ... / تقضي المحكمة المختصة التي تنظر دعوى البطلان من تلقاء نفسها ببطلان حكم التحكيم إذا تضمن ما يخالف أحكام الشريعة الإسلامية والنظام العام في المملكة، أو ما اتفق عليه طرفا التحكيم، أو إذا وجدت أن موضوع النزاع من المسائل التي لا يجوز التحكيم فيها. | Closed list of grounds plus ex officio Sharia/public-order review; ground (d) makes a tribunal's failure to apply the chosen law an annulment ground, which is broader than the Model Law. The 1447H amendment to (b) is a wording change only. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` (in-force text) |
references/jurisdictions/ksa/arbitration-law.md:54:| Law Art. 51; Regs Arts. 17(1), 18 | The annulment action is brought by either party within 60 days following notification of the award; a waiver of the right to bring it made before the award does not bar the action (Regs: a waiver after the award does). If the court upholds the award it must order its enforcement, by a judgment not subject to any appeal; if it annuls the award, its judgment may be appealed within 30 days from the day after notification (Regs: to the Supreme Court). The applicant files the original or certified copy of the award, a true copy of the arbitration agreement and a certified Arabic translation if needed. | ترفع دعوى بطلان حكم التحكيم من أي من طرفيه خلال الستين يوماً التالية لتاريخ إبلاغ ذلك الطرف بالحكم. ولا يحول تنازل مدعي البطلان عن حقه في رفعها قبل صدور حكم التحكيم دون قبول الدعوى. / إذا حكمت المحكمة المختصة بتأييد حكم التحكيم وجب عليها أن تأمر بتنفيذه، ويكون حكمها في ذلك غير قابل للطعن ... أما إذا حكمت ببطلان حكم التحكيم، فيكون حكمها قابلاً للطعن خلال ثلاثين يوماً. | Confirmed 60-day window from notification; "exclusion of recourse" clauses in the contract are ineffective. Asymmetric finality: an upheld award is final at once, an annulment can go to the Supreme Court. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` |

