labor-law.md
67 | Art. 83 (M/46) | (1) If the work lets the worker know the employer's clients, the employer may, to protect its legitimate interests, require him not to compete after the contract ends; to be valid the condition must be in writing and specific as to time, place and type of work, and its duration may not exceed two years from the end of the relationship. (2) If the work gives access to the employer's business secrets, the employer may require non-disclosure after the contract ends; to be valid the condition must be in writing and specific as to time, place and type of work. (3) By exception to the Law, the employer may sue within one year from the date of discovering the worker's breach of either obligation | جاز لصاحب العمل – حمايةً لمصالحه المشروعة – أن يشترط على العامل ألا يقوم بعد انتهاء العقد بمنافسته، ويجب لصحة هذا الشرط أن يكون مُحرراً ومُحدداً، من حيث الزمان والمكان ونوع العمل، ويجب ألا تزيد مدته على سنتين من تاريخ انتهاء العلاقة بين الطرفين ... لصاحب العمل رفع دعوى خلال سنة من تاريخ اكتشاف مخالفة العامل | Non-compete drafting: written; named territory; named type of work; term ≤ 2 years; justified by client knowledge or secrets. A non-compete with no geography or no defined activity, or one longer than two years, fails the validity test. Post-termination confidentiality also needs a stated time, place and type of work (an indefinite NDA clause is at risk). The Law does not require consideration or a penalty amount; penalty clauses are commonly used and courts may reduce them `[model knowledge — verify]`. Limitation for the employer's claim: one year from discovery (an exception to Art. 234's 12 months from termination). HRSD Regs Art. 27 extends Art. 83 to flexible-work (العمل المرن) contracts `[authority — HRSD]` | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` `[BOE — official English]` `[authority — HRSD]` |
government-tenders-procurement-law.md
30 | Art. 1 (definitions), Art. 10, Art. 11, Art. 93 — **who is bound** | "Government entities" are ministries, government agencies, authorities, public departments and institutions, and bodies with independent public legal personality. The Law applies to all government entities (Art. 10) and to their works and procurement executed outside the Kingdom, with possible partial exemptions per the Regulations (Art. 11). Companies executing works and procurement on behalf of government entities must apply the Law (Art. 93). | الجهات الحكومية: الوزارات والأجهزة الحكومية والهيئات والمصالح والمؤسسات العامة والأجهزة ذات الشخصية المعنوية العامة المستقلة. / يطبق النظام على جميع الجهات الحكومية. / تلتزم الشركات التي تنفذ الأعمال والمشتريات نيابة عن الجهات الحكومية بتطبيق أحكام النظام. | The test is public legal personality, not state ownership. `[model knowledge — verify]`: state-owned joint-stock companies (stc, Aramco, SABIC, SEC, Ma'aden) and PIF portfolio companies are generally NOT bound and contract under their own procurement manuals and standard terms, which often copy GTPL mechanics (bonds, 10% delay caps, Etimad-style portals) by contract rather than by law; a contract with such a company should be reviewed as a private contract with those terms, and this flag must be confirmed per counterparty. Art. 93 captures development companies and project vehicles acting as the government's agent. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]`; state-owned-company position `[model knowledge — verify]` |
47 | Art. 72 — **delay penalty cap** | If the contractor is late in performing the contract beyond the specified date, a delay penalty is imposed not exceeding 6% of the value of a supply contract and not exceeding 20% of the value of other contracts; the percentages may be increased with the Minister's prior approval provided the increase is disclosed to bidders before they bid. | إذا تأخر المتعاقد في تنفيذ العقد عن الموعد المحدد؛ تفرض عليه غرامة تأخير لا تتجاوز (6%) من قيمة عقد التوريد، ولا تتجاوز (20%) من قيمة العقود الأخرى، ويجوز زيادة تلك النسب بموافقة مسبقة من الوزير، على أن توضح تلك الزيادة للمتنافسين قبل تقديم عروضهم. | Confirmed: Art. 72; 6% of contract value for supply contracts; 20% for all other contracts (works, services, consultancy); higher caps only with the Minister's prior approval disclosed in the tender. The Law states the cap by reference to "قيمة العقد" (contract value) and says nothing about computing the penalty on the delayed portion. `[model knowledge — verify]`: the Implementing Regulations (recalled as Art. 122) provide that the penalty is calculated on the value of the delayed works or items where the delivered part can be used independently of the delayed part, and on the whole where it cannot; the daily/weekly rate is set in the contract and the model contracts, and the penalty is deducted from progress payments or the bond without proof of loss. Treat the delayed-portion rule as unconfirmed until the Regulations article is read. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` for the caps; delayed-portion computation `[model knowledge — verify]` |
commercial-agencies-law.md
30 | Art. 1 (unamended) | Non-Saudis, whether natural or legal persons, may not be commercial agents in the Kingdom. Saudi companies carrying on commercial agency business must have wholly Saudi capital, and their board members and authorised signatories must be Saudi. | لا يجوز لغير السعوديين سواء بصفة أشخاص طبيعيين أو معنويين أن يكونوا وكلاء تجاريين في المملكة العربية السعودية، على أن الشركات السعودية التي تقوم بأعمال الوكالات التجارية يجب أن يكون رأس مالها بالكامل سعودياً، وأن يكون أعضاء مجالس إدارتها ومن لهم حق التوقيع باسمها سعوديين. | On the face of the Law, which the portal shows as unamended on this point, a MISA-licensed foreign-owned LLC cannot be registered as a commercial agent, and a Saudi JV with a foreign shareholder is also excluded. `[model knowledge — verify]`: the Ministry of Commerce has, through amendments to the Implementing Regulations and its electronic "commercial agencies" service (2023-2024), permitted foreign-invested companies licensed by MISA to register agencies, and wholesale/retail trade is open to 100% foreign ownership under conditions; whether this rests on regulation, ministerial exception or non-enforcement of Art. 1 must be confirmed with counsel because the statute has not been amended. A foreign principal selling directly through its own licensed Saudi subsidiary is not "a commercial agent" and this article does not stop it. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]`; relaxation `[model knowledge — verify]` |
32 | Art. 3 (unamended), first sentence | No one may carry on the work of a commercial agent unless entered in the register kept for that purpose at the Ministry of Commerce; the Minister creates the register by decision. | لا يجوز أن يقوم بعمل الوكيل التجاري إلا من كان مقيداً في السجل المعد لهذا الغرض في وزارة التجارة والصناعة. | Registration is a condition of lawfully *acting* as an agent or distributor (see the 1400H Added Art. 1 row), not a condition of the validity of the contract between principal and agent (see Art. 4 row). The Law does not itself fix a deadline; `[model knowledge — verify]`: the Implementing Regulations require the agent/distributor to apply for registration within three months of signing the agreement, and late applications have been treated as violations attracting the Art. 4 fine. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]`; three-month deadline `[model knowledge — verify]` |
33 | Art. 3, register contents | The register records the name of the merchant or company, the type of goods covered, the principal company or establishment, the date of the appointment and its term if the agency is for a fixed period. | تشتمل بيانات السجل المذكور على اسم التاجر أو الشركة، ونوع البضاعة الموكل فيها، والشركة والمؤسسة الموكلة، وتاريخ التوكيل، ومدته إن كانت الوكالة محددة بأجل. | Diligence on a Saudi distributor should ask for the registration certificate for each principal/product line: it evidences the principal, the goods and the term. A new product line, a change of principal or a renewal needs an updated entry `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` |
34 | Art. 3, application, refusal, appeal | Applications with supporting documents go to the Deputy Minister. Registration may be refused only to a non-Saudi or to a Saudi barred from or unfit to practise trade; a refused applicant may appeal to the Minister. | لا يجوز رفض القيد إلا لغير السعودي أو لمن كان سعودياً ممنوعاً من مزاولة التجارة وغير أهل لممارستها، ويجوز لمن رفض قيده أن يتظلم إلى وزير التجارة والصناعة. | The Ministry has no discretion under the Law to refuse a qualifying Saudi applicant on commercial grounds (for example because another agent is already registered for the same product), which is the textual basis for saying the Law imposes no exclusivity. `[model knowledge — verify]`: the Regulations historically required the application to attach the agency contract (in or conforming to the Ministry's model form, see Added Art. 4) and a certified, legalised copy from the principal; the current electronic service accepts the parties' own contract with the required data fields. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]`; documentary requirements `[model knowledge — verify]` |
38 | Added Art. 1 (Royal Decree M/32 of 10/8/1400H) — **distributors are inside the Law** | Without prejudice to other laws, the Commercial Agencies Law and its amendments apply to everyone who contracts with the producer, or with whoever stands in the producer's place in its country, to carry on commercial business, whether as agent or as distributor in any form of agency or distribution. | مع عدم الإخلال بأية أنظمة أخرى يسري نظام الوكالات التجارية الصادر بالمرسوم الملكي رقم (11) وتاريخ 20/ 2 /1382هـ، وتعديلاته على كل من يتعاقد مع المنتج أو من يقوم مقامه في بلده للقيام بالأعمال التجارية سواء كان وكيلاً أو موزعاً بأية صورة من صور الوكالة أو التوزيع. | Confirmed from the statute: a foreign principal signing a distribution agreement with a Saudi distributor triggers the Law (nationality rule, registration, penalties, spare-parts duty) for the distributor. Buy-sell distributorships, dealerships and exclusive resellers are all "distribution in any form". The principal has no registration duty of its own, but will be asked for a legalised appointment letter or signed contract for the filing. Whether a reseller of services (as opposed to a producer's goods) is covered turns on "المنتج" and is not settled by the text. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` |
39 | Added Art. 2 and para. "ثالثاً" (Royal Decree M/32 of 10/8/1400H) — **spare parts and maintenance** | Without prejudice to other rules on maintenance and spare parts, the agent and the distributor must: (a) permanently secure the spare parts consumers usually demand for the products of the agency, and other spare parts within a reasonable period, per the Regulations; (b) secure the necessary maintenance for the products and guarantee manufacturing quality and the conditions producers usually set, continuously throughout the agency and for one year after its expiry or the appointment of a new agent, whichever is earlier, per the Regulations. Paragraph "ثالثاً" of the decree extends Added Art. 2 to importers even if they are not agents or distributors, and to anyone who makes selling (directly or through others) a trade for profit, with the same penalties. | يلتزم الوكيل والموزع بما يلي: أ) أن يؤمن بصفة دائمة قطع الغيار التي يطلبها المستهلكون عادة ... ب) تأمين الصيانة اللازمة للمنتجات وضمان جودة الصنع ... وذلك بصفة مستمرة طوال مدة الوكالة ولمدة سنة تالية لتاريخ انتهائها أو لتاريخ تعيين وكيل جديد أيهما أسبق. | The Saudi agent or distributor carries a statutory after-sales duty to end customers that outlives the contract by a year; a distribution agreement should therefore allocate spare-parts supply, warranty support and post-termination run-off between principal and distributor, because the distributor's exposure to the Art. 4 fine and to consumer claims does not end when the principal appoints a successor. Importers and professional resellers who are not registered agents carry the same duty. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` |

