15:| Official source (authoritative language) | https://laws.boe.gov.sa/BoeLaws/Laws/LawDetails/38334008-3b70-4c6c-b3af-aba3016a8061/1 ; Regulations (MoJ, file labelled draft): https://www.moj.gov.sa/Documents/ProjectExecution.pdf |
17:| Text last read from the official source | 2026-09-04 (Law, Arabic, 96 articles plus Decree and Decision text; Regulations draft, Arabic, Arts. 1–351 read for Arts. 1–340) |
28:| Article | Rule (English) | Rule (authoritative language) | Practical effect | Tag |
30:| Art. 2; Regs Art. 2 | The Law and Regulations apply to the commercial court and the cases within its jurisdiction, without prejudice to the commercial laws and international conventions to which the Kingdom is party. The Regulations set the order of application: (a) the international convention, (b) the special procedural text in a commercial law, (c) the Law and Regulations. | دون إخلال بما نصت عليه الأنظمة التجارية والاتفاقيات الدولية التي تكون المملكة طرفاً فيها، تسري أحكام النظام واللائحة على المحكمة والدعاوى التي تختص بنظرها. / يكون تطبيق أحكام المادة الثانية من النظام وفق الترتيب الآتي: النص الوارد في الاتفاقية الدولية، النص الإجرائي الخاص في الأنظمة التجارية، النص الوارد في النظام واللائحة. | A special procedure in the Companies Law, Bankruptcy Law or an IP law displaces the general commercial-court procedure; a treaty (e.g. a bilateral judicial cooperation agreement) ranks above both. Skills should check the sector law before assuming these timelines. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` (Law) / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
31:| Art. 6; Regs Arts. 10–13 | By exception to the Law and the Law of Civil Procedure, and without prejudice to public order and the rules of justice, parties to a commercial dealing who are all merchants may agree on specific pleading procedures. The Regulations require any agreement the Law or Regulations refer to be in writing; the agreement may cover the number of memoranda, notice procedures, document deadlines, a named expert or expert procedure (including agreeing to accept an expert's opinion), and shortening (never lengthening) procedural periods other than the court's own; it must be invoked at the first hearing or the right lapses; parties may also agree a case plan for the court's approval. | للأطراف في التعامل التجاري - متى كان كل منهم تاجراً - الاتفاق على إجراءات محددة للترافع وما يتصل به. / يجب أن يكون الاتفاق مكتوباً ... تقليص أي مدد إجرائية ... ولا يجوز للأطراف الاتفاق على مدة تتجاوز المدد المنصوص عليها ... يجب التمسك بوجود اتفاق على إجراءات محددة للترافع في أول جلسة؛ وإلا سقط الحق في التمسك به. | A B2B contract can validly pre-agree litigation mechanics (e.g. a single joint expert, capped memoranda) for a Saudi commercial-court dispute, but only between merchants and only to accelerate, not to slow down. A dispute-resolution clause that attempts to extend statutory periods is ineffective on this point. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
32:| Art. 7; Regs Arts. 38–47 | Any procedure under the Law may be electronic, including filing and registering claims and requests, hearing them, remote pleading, exchange of memoranda, judgment and objection. The Regulations give an electronic act the same effects as a physical one, permit AI tools, bar a party from denying an opponent's submission merely because it was electronic, route e-litigation through the Ministry's approved systems, allow electronic verification in place of signature, and permit remote hearings in all cases subject to the Ministry's approved means and publicity (a non-merchant party may ask for an in-court hearing within one day of being notified). | يجوز أن يكون أي من الإجراءات المنصوص عليها في النظام إلكترونيًّا، بما في ذلك تقديم الدعاوى والطلبات وقيدها، ونظرها، والترافع عن بُعد، وتبادل المذكرات، والحكم، والاعتراض. / يترتب على الإجراء المتخذ إلكترونياً الآثار ذاتها ... يجوز أن يكتفى عن التوقيع ... بوسائل التحقق الإلكترونية. | Commercial litigation runs on the Ministry of Justice's Najiz platform in practice; time stamps follow the court's time zone (Regs Art. 43) and electronic deadlines expire at 23:59 (Regs Art. 5). The platform name "Najiz" is not in the text. `[model knowledge — verify]` | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
33:| Art. 8(1); Regs Arts. 100–107, 327 | The Regulations determine conciliation and mediation procedures, including the cases in which conciliation/mediation must precede the hearing, not to exceed 30 days from commencement unless the parties agree a longer period. The draft Regulations require prior conciliation/mediation before registering: (a) single-judge cases (Regs Art. 17), (b) Art. 16(3) claims (drafted as mudaraba partner disputes; since Royal Decree M/191 of 1444H the paragraph covers partnership-contract disputes under the Civil Transactions Law), (c) cases between spouses or relatives to the fourth degree, (d) cases on contracts containing a written agreement to attempt conciliation, mediation or amicable settlement before litigation, (e) other categories the court president designates. Compliance is shown by a certificate that conciliation ended without (or with partial) settlement, or by proof of applying and the period having elapsed. Small claims: prior conciliation not exceeding 15 days. A settlement reached after registration is recorded and takes the force of an enforcement instrument. | تحدد اللائحة إجراءات المصالحة والوساطة، بما في ذلك الدعاوى التي يجب أن يسبق نظرَها اللجوءُ إلى المصالحة والوساطة، على ألا تزيد مدة تلك الإجراءات على (ثلاثين) يوماً. / يجب اللجوء إلى المصالحة والوساطة قبل قيد أي من الدعاوى الآتية: ... الدعاوى المتعلقة بالعقود التي تتضمن الاتفاق كتابة على اللجوء إلى المصالحة والوساطة والتسوية الودية قبل اللجوء إلى القضاء. | A contractual multi-tier clause (negotiation/mediation before court) is given procedural teeth: the commercial court will not register the claim until the attempt is evidenced. Draft a fixed, short attempt period; the court-side cap is 30 days unless the parties agreed longer. Whether the approved regulation kept this list must be confirmed. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` (Art. 8) / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
34:| Arts. 9–12; Regs Arts. 71–83 | Valid service addresses include: the verified or chosen electronic address; residence; the address registered with the postal authority; the commercial-register address for that activity; the address stated in the case papers; **the address stated in the contract, for disputes arising from that contract**; and an address chosen by a foreigner in the Kingdom. A party may designate a lawyer's address. Change of the case-papers address must be notified within 48 hours or service there remains effective. Electronic service is by SMS to the verified mobile, verified/chosen e-mail, or notification through a government e-account; other addresses are served through a licensed postal provider. A person resident abroad may be served under these rules where the parties have so agreed, without prejudice to international conventions; the Regulations require that address to be recorded in a document between the parties, provide diplomatic-channel service where that fails, and treat the contract address as valid for five years from the contract unless agreed otherwise. Legal persons: service on the legal representative, a general partner, the manager, the legal department, or a branch manager for branch disputes; foreign companies with a branch or commercial representative: on that branch manager or representative. | يعد عنواناً للتبليغ ... العنوان المدون في العقد محل التعامل في المنازعات الناشئة عن ذلك العقد ... على الطرف حال تغييره العنوان ... أن يبلغ المحكمة خلال (ثمانٍ وأربعين) ساعة. / دون إخلال بالاتفاقيات الدولية، يجوز تبليغ من يكون محل إقامته خارج المملكة ... متى وجد اتفاق بين الأطراف على ذلك. / لا تسري أحكام الفقرة (1/و) من المادة التاسعة من النظام بعد انقضاء خمس سنوات من تاريخ العقد ما لم يتفق الأطراف على خلاف ذلك. | The notices clause of a contract is also the service clause for Saudi litigation: a stale address in the contract can carry valid service for five years. Foreign counterparties should be advised that agreeing to service at a contract address (including e-mail) enables service abroad without letters rogatory. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
35:| Art. 13; Regs Arts. 89–93 | The court may fine a party up to SAR 10,000 for breach of case procedure or hearing order (final). Case data, papers and documents of commercial cases are open to the public for a fee equal to the cost of the service; on application by an interested person the court may declare certain papers or documents confidential vis-à-vis persons other than the court, without prejudice to the publicity of hearings. The Regulations treat a document as confidential where a law or competent-authority decision so provides, where the parties' agreement makes it confidential, or where access would infringe a trade secret; confidentiality cannot be claimed if the parties previously agreed there is none; the court's decision on confidentiality is not subject to any objection. | للمحكمة عند إخلال أحد الأطراف ... أن تأمر بفرض غرامة لا تتجاوز عشرة آلاف ريال ... يتاح اطلاع العموم على بيانات الدعاوى التجارية وأوراقها ومستنداتها لقاء مقابل مالي ... ويجوز - بناءً على طلب ذي مصلحة - تقرير سرية بعض أوراق الدعوى التجارية أو مستنداتها لغير المحكمة. | Commercial-court filings are public by default. A contractual confidentiality clause is a recognised ground for a sealing order under the draft Regulations, so NDA and MSA confidentiality clauses should expressly cover litigation filings and require the party filing to seek confidentiality. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
36:| Art. 15 | Absent a special text in the commercial laws or in treaties and conventions to which the Kingdom is party, the international-jurisdiction rules of the Law of Civil Procedure apply to cases within the commercial court's jurisdiction. | فيما لم يرد فيه نص خاص في الأنظمة التجارية، أو المعاهدات والاتفاقيات الدولية التي تكون المملكة طرفًا فيها، تسري قواعد الاختصاص الدولي المنصوص عليها في نظام المرافعات الشرعية. | Whether a Saudi commercial court will take jurisdiction over a foreign defendant is answered by the Law of Civil Procedure (generally: defendant domiciled or resident in the Kingdom, obligation to be performed in the Kingdom, etc.). Those rules are not in this file. `[model knowledge — verify]` | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` |
37:| Art. 16 (marked amended on the portal); Regs Arts. 48–50 | The commercial court has jurisdiction over: (1) disputes between merchants arising from their original or ancillary commercial activities; (2) claims against a merchant in commercial-contract disputes where the principal claim exceeds SAR 100,000 in the text read today (the Supreme Judicial Council may raise this figure); (3) as amended by Royal Decree M/191 of 29/11/1444H, disputes arising from the partnership contracts (عقود المشاركة) provided for in the Civil Transactions Law (original text: disputes between partners in a mudaraba); (4) claims and violations under the Companies Law; (5) under the Bankruptcy Law; (6) under the intellectual-property laws; (7) under the other commercial laws; (8) claims and requests concerning judicial custodians, trustees, liquidators and appointed experts where linked to a case within its jurisdiction; (9) compensation claims for harm arising from a case previously heard by the court. The draft Regulations: item (2) requires a contractual relationship (Regs Art. 48) and, in Regs Art. 49, states the threshold as SAR 500,000; item (3) requires a written contract (Regs Art. 50, drafted against the original mudaraba wording). | تختص المحكمة بالنظر في الآتي: المنازعات التي تنشأ بين التجار بسبب أعمالهم التجارية الأصلية أو التبعية. الدعاوى المقامة على التاجر في منازعات العقود التجارية، متى كانت قيمة المطالبة الأصلية في الدعوى تزيد على مائة ألف ريال، وللمجلس عند الاقتضاء زيادة هذه القيمة. المنازعات التي تنشأ عن عقود المشاركة المنصوص عليها في نظام المعاملات المدنية (النص النافذ بموجب المرسوم الملكي رقم م/191 وتاريخ 29/11/1444هـ؛ النص الأصلي: منازعات الشركاء في شركة المضاربة). الدعاوى والمخالفات الناشئة عن تطبيق أحكام نظام الشركات ... نظام الإفلاس ... أنظمة الملكية الفكرية ... الأنظمة التجارية الأخرى ... | Merchant-to-merchant contract claims go to the commercial court regardless of value. A non-merchant's claim against a merchant on a commercial contract goes to the commercial court only above the threshold; the Law text in force says SAR 100,000 (the M/191 amendment touched only paragraph (3)) while the draft Regulations say SAR 500,000, so whether the Council has raised the figure must be confirmed before any routing advice. Partnership-contract disputes under the Civil Transactions Law (including mudaraba as one form) are now expressly commercial-court matters. Company-law claims (shareholder disputes, director liability) and bankruptcy matters are commercial-court matters; Regs Art. 8 measures the claim by the sums in the statement of claim excluding costs and fees, or by the value of the underlying obligation for non-monetary relief. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` (in-force text including the M/191 amendment to paragraph (3)); threshold conflict flagged; `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
38:| Art. 17; Regs Arts. 51–55 | Unless the parties agree otherwise in writing, territorial jurisdiction lies with the court of the defendant's place of residence; if none in the Kingdom, the claimant's; the claim may also be brought where the contract was concluded, performed or was to be performed. Company cases: the court of the company's head office (claims against the company, by the company against a partner, between partners, or against managers/board members); branch-contract disputes may be brought where the branch is. The plea of lack of territorial jurisdiction is lost once the party makes any request or defence, including at the case-preparation stage. | ما لم يتفق الطرفان كتابة على غير ذلك ... يكون الاختصاص المكاني للمحكمة التي يقع في نطاق اختصاصها مكان إقامة المدعى عليه ... ويجوز أن تقام الدعوى في المحكمة التي أبرم العقد أو نفذ أو كان واجب التنفيذ في نطاقها. / في الدعاوى المتعلقة بالشركات، يكون الاختصاص المكاني للمحكمة التي يقع في نطاق اختصاصها المقر الرئيس للشركة. | A written venue clause choosing a particular Saudi commercial court (e.g. Riyadh) is effective; venue is optional, not exclusive, absent agreement. Raise a venue objection in the very first submission. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
39:| Art. 18; Regs Arts. 54, 56–57 | The court may rule separately on a plea of lack of subject-matter jurisdiction within 20 days of the plea. The Regulations add an administrative jurisdiction report within two working days of registration and a circuit decision within three working days, referral of a no-jurisdiction judgment to appeal the day after filing, and extend Art. 18 to pleas of lack of judicial (ولائي) and territorial jurisdiction. | للمحكمة أن تفصل استقلالاً في الدفع بعدم الاختصاص النوعي في مدة لا تتجاوز (عشرين) يوماً من تاريخ الدفع. | Jurisdiction fights are front-loaded and fast; see Art. 79(2)–(4) for the 10-day appeal and finality of the resulting judgment. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
40:| Art. 19; Regs Arts. 116–121 | In the cases the Regulations specify, the claimant must notify the defendant in writing to perform the claimed right at least 15 days before filing. Before registration, and under court supervision, the parties may undertake conciliation/mediation, exchange of documents and memoranda, or a meeting to define claims, defences and evidence, documented as the Regulations provide. Draft Regulations: the notice is required in all cases within the court's jurisdiction except penalty cases under commercial laws, cases with an administrative body as party, small claims and urgent requests; it must state the parties, subject, claims and supporting document, with proof attached to the statement of claim (failing which the cure procedure of Art. 21 applies); proof of a prior attempt at amicable settlement, conciliation or mediation counts as the notice once the 15-day period has elapsed. | يجب في الدعاوى التي تحددها اللائحة أن يخطر المدعي المدعى عليه كتابة بأداء الحق المدعى به قبل (خمسة عشر) يوماً على الأقل من إقامة الدعوى. / يعد في حكم الإخطار تقديم ما يثبت اللجوء إلى التسوية الودية والمصالحة والوساطة قبل قيد الدعوى بشرط مضي المدة. | Send a formal demand (through a traceable channel) at least 15 days before filing; a contractual notice-of-breach step, if evidenced, does double duty. Pre-filing exchange under Art. 19(2) also interrupts the five-year non-hearing period (Regs Art. 63) and shortens small-claims timelines (Regs Art. 324). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
41:| Arts. 20–23; Regs Arts. 94–99, 131–136 | Claims are brought by a statement of claim filed with the court; the Regulations determine which claims must be filed by a lawyer. The statement must give the parties' details and addresses, enumerate the claims and all grounds; unrelated claims may not be joined. Registration is by the competent administration; deficiencies must be cured within 15 days (registration then dates back to the filing), with a 15-day grievance to the court president (final). The defendant must lodge a defence memorandum with the answer, all pleas, claims and grounds at least one day before the hearing (urgent requests excepted). Draft Regulations: all claims must be filed by a lawyer except Art. 16(2), (8), (9) claims and small claims; pleading by a lawyer is mandatory above SAR 10m (items 1, 2, 8, 9) or SAR 2m (items 3, 4, 6, 7) and in financial-restructuring bankruptcy applications; licensed in-house legal departments of private legal persons and representatives of administrative bodies may act; the first hearing is set within 20 days of registration and at least four days after service (24 hours in urgent cases). | ترفع الدعوى بصحيفة تودع لدى المحكمة، وتحدد اللائحة الدعاوى التي يجب رفعها من محامٍ ... لا يجمع في صحيفة الدعوى بين عدة طلبات لا رابط بينها. / على المدعى عليه ... أن يودع لدى المحكمة مذكرة بدفاعه مشتملة على جوابه على الدعوى وجميع دفوعه ... قبل الجلسة المحددة لنظر الدعوى بيوم واحد على الأقل. | Front-loaded pleading: the defence must be complete before the first hearing, and a late-produced defence can be refused (Art. 26). In-house counsel can appear only if licensed by the Ministry. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
42:| Art. 24; Regs Arts. 58–67 | Absent a special text, claims within the court's jurisdiction are not heard after five years from the date the claimed right arose, unless the defendant acknowledges the right or the claimant shows an excuse the court accepts. Draft Regulations: rights arising before the Law run from its entry into force; the period cannot be varied by agreement; waiver of the plea is valid only after the period has run; the period starts when the debt falls due; "excuse" includes a material or moral impediment for its duration; a judicial claim (even before an incompetent court) or an Art. 19(2) pre-filing step interrupts the period; the plea belongs to the debtor and is not raised by the court of its own motion; it may be raised at any stage including on appeal; abandoned or annulled claims count towards the period; non-hearing of the principal claim extends to dependent claims such as against a guarantor. | فيما لم يرد به نص خاص، لا تسمع الدعاوى التي تختص بنظرها المحكمة بعد مضي (خمس) سنوات من تاريخ نشوء الحق المدعى به، ما لم يقر المدعى عليه بالحق أو يتقدم المدعي بعذر تقبله المحكمة. / لا يقبل الاتفاق على خلاف المدة المحددة نظاماً لسماع الدعوى. | Five years is the working limitation period for commercial claims in the commercial court; a contractual limitation clause (longer or shorter) is not effective under the draft Regulations. Diligence on receivables and claims older than five years should treat them as at risk. Cross-check the Civil Transactions Law's own non-hearing periods where that law applies. `[model knowledge — verify]` | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
43:| Arts. 25–28; Regs Arts. 68–70, 145–151 | Proceedings and pleading are in writing, though the circuit may hear the parties orally and must record an oral summary on request; the court may fine or refuse counter/incidental claims from a party who fails to file on time without excuse; adjournment only for a recorded reason and never twice for the same reason; a circuit may delegate preparation of the case to one of its judges. Draft Regulations: statutory periods may be exceeded only for necessity by reasoned decision; maximum duration 180 days at first instance (small claims excepted), 20 days for appeal without hearing, 90 days for appeal with hearing; a pre-trial meeting checks jurisdiction, offers settlement, fixes the issues, evidence, witness list and timetable; at most two pleading hearings after service of the defendant; adjournment after the first hearing not more than 30 days. | تكون إجراءات نظر الدعوى والمرافعة فيها كتابة ... لا يجوز تأجيل الجلسة إلا لسبب يقتضي ذلك يثبت في محضرها، ولا يجوز التأجيل للسبب نفسه أكثر من مرة. / يكون الحد الأقصى للفصل في القضية ... مائة وثمانون يوماً في الدعاوى المقامة أمام الدرجة الابتدائية عدا الدعاوى اليسيرة. | Plan on roughly six months to a first-instance judgment and three further months on appeal with a hearing, if the draft timetable is the approved one; expert referrals add up to 90 days (Regs Art. 278). Timelines are court-side maxima, not guarantees. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
44:| Art. 29(2); Regs Arts. 104–107 | If the parties settle before the circuit, the settlement is recorded in the hearing minutes, signed by the parties and approved by the presiding judge; the approved minutes are an enforcement instrument (سند تنفيذي), a copy is delivered as for judgments and the case ends. The Regulations extend this to settlements at any stage, even after closing of pleadings or before the appeal court, and to a settlement recorded before the competent administration, and require a copy where the settlement is embodied in an enforcement instrument under the Enforcement Law. | إذا اتفق الأطراف على الصلح أمام الدائرة أثبت ذلك في محضر الجلسة، ويوقع الأطراف عليه، ويعتمده رئيس الجلسة، ويعد محضر الجلسة المعتمد سنداً تنفيذيًّا. | A court-recorded settlement is directly enforceable through the enforcement court without a fresh action (see `enforcement-law.md`, Art. 7(1)(c)). Settlement agreements reached in litigation should be recorded in the minutes rather than left as private contracts. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
45:| Arts. 30–32; Regs Arts. 154–160 | A defendant served personally (or through a representative), or who attends any hearing or files a defence, is treated as present even if absent later; if served other than personally and absent, the case is adjourned once and re-served, after which judgment is treated as adversarial; service on a legal person under the Law is always personal service. A claimant absent without accepted excuse: judgment on the defendant's request if the case is ripe, otherwise striking out, with 30 days to apply to resume, failing which the case is deemed never brought. Draft Regulations: a party is absent if not present within 30 minutes of the scheduled time; a defendant served who fails to appear loses the right to raise temporary (procedural) pleas. | إذا تبلغ المدعى عليه لشخصه أو وكليه، أو حضر أي منهما في أي جلسة أمام المحكمة، أو قدم مذكرة بدفاعه، عُدَّت الخصومة حضورية ... في جميع الأحوال، يعد تبليغ الشخصية الاعتبارية - بموجب أحكام النظام - تبليغاً لشخصها. | Companies cannot rely on defective-service defences once served at any Art. 9/11 address; default judgments against corporate defendants are adversarial and appealable only within the ordinary period. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
46:| Arts. 33–37; Regs Arts. 161–177 | Urgent requests (الطلبات المستعجلة) are heard by a single-judge circuit established by the Council, referred immediately and decided within three working days of referral, if necessary in the applicant's presence without the other party. They include: inspection to establish a state of affairs, travel ban, stopping new works, judicial custody, precautionary attachment, obtaining a product sample, preserving specified documents, prohibiting or permitting a disposal, and requests given urgent character by the commercial laws. The order lapses if the main claim is not filed within seven days, if the claim is abandoned or deemed not brought, or if the claimant fails on the merits; any interested person may seek cancellation where urgency has ceased, the case is stayed, interrupted or struck out. The court may require security to compensate the respondent if the applicant proves not entitled, with compensation decided in the merits judgment. Draft Regulations: an urgent request is a matter where delay is feared, without touching the merits; it may be filed before or after the main action; ex parte determination where surprise is needed, with immediate service of the order; a travel-ban request must be accompanied by security of 5% of the principal claim and not less than SAR 50,000; the person banned may lodge security for the claimed amount and is then allowed to travel; urgent decisions are always appealable. | يُحال الطلب المستعجل إلى الدائرة المختصة فور تقديمه، ويُفصل فيه خلال مدة لا تتجاوز (ثلاثة) أيام عمل من تاريخ إحالته، ويجوز - عند الاقتضاء - الفصل في الطلب بحضور مقدمه دون حضور الطرف الآخر. / تشمل الطلبات المستعجلة ما يأتي: المعاينة لإثبات الحالة. المنع من السفر. وقف الأعمال الجديدة. الحراسة القضائية. الحجز التحفظي. الحصول على عينة من منتج. التحفظ على مستندات معينة. المنع من التصرف أو الإذن به. | Interim relief is available fast and, where surprise matters, ex parte, but it is parasitic on a main claim filed within seven days. Precautionary attachment substance is still governed by the 1433H Enforcement Law's attachment chapter until it is moved into the Law of Civil Procedure (see `enforcement-law.md`, Decree ¶6). Travel bans against foreign executives require real security. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
47:| Art. 38 | Absent a special text in the commercial laws, the evidence chapter applies to cases within the court's jurisdiction; no particular form is required to prove an obligation unless the parties agree otherwise; the court may rely on evidentiary procedures conducted in a foreign state unless contrary to public order; where the parties agree specific evidence rules the court applies them, subject to public order; absent a special text, the burden of proof may be shifted by agreement. | لا يلزم لإثبات الالتزام شكل خاص، ما لم تتفق الأطراف على غير ذلك. للمحكمة أن تعتدّ بإجراءات الإثبات التي جرت في دولة أجنبية ما لم تخالف أحكام النظام العام. دون إخلال بالنظام العام، إذا اتفق الأطراف على قواعد محددة في الإثبات؛ فَتُعمِل المحكمة اتفاقَهم. فيما لم يرد فيه نص خاص، يجوز الاتفاق على نقل عبء الإثبات. | Contractual evidence clauses ("entire agreement", "records conclusive absent manifest error", burden-shifting warranties) are given effect in commercial-court litigation subject to public order. Foreign depositions or discovery outputs can be relied on. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` |
48:| Arts. 42–47; Regs Arts. 232–238 | Statements in official documents bind their maker unless disproved; a private document is deemed to emanate from the person it is attributed to unless that person expressly denies the handwriting, signature, seal or fingerprint (the denial must specify its basis; a party who discussed the document's content cannot later deny it); a copy is deemed to match the original unless disputed, and disputed copies may still serve as presumptions in listed cases; signed or attributable correspondence has the force of a private document. A party may request specific or categorised documents held by the other party that relate to the commercial dealing and are not confidential; refusal to produce what the court orders is a presumption against the refusing party, who may not rely on the withheld document; the court may join a third party or order a government body to produce relevant documents; a document-recovery request is available to an interested person. | لأي من الأطراف حق طلب ما لدى الطرف الآخر من مستندات ذات صلة بالدعوى أو الاطلاع عليها ... أن تكون المستندات محددة بذاتها أو أنواعها ... ألا يكون لها طابع السريَّة ... فللمحكمة أن تعد امتناعه قرينة. | Targeted document production exists but is narrower than common-law disclosure: requests must identify documents or classes, and contractual confidentiality (Regs Art. 89) is a ground for refusal. Disclosure carve-outs in NDAs for "legally compelled" production remain necessary. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
49:| Art. 55; Regs Arts. 260–264 | Electronic evidence may be treated as proof; it includes electronic records/documents, electronic media, means of communication, e-mail, electronic registers and any other electronic evidence the Regulations specify. Draft Regulations: electronic evidence embodying an official or private document has the same legal effect; evidence from electronic media is valid only if created with the other party's consent or knowledge; it is probative where issued under the Electronic Transactions Law, through a means verified with a government or licensed body or licensed notary, where the contract specified the electronic means, where the opponent discussed its content before denying it, or where drawn from the opponent's public communication channel; the court may appoint an expert to verify it. | يجوز اعتبار الدليل الإلكتروني حجة في الإثبات ... يشمل الدليل الإلكتروني الآتي: المحرر الإلكتروني. الوسائط الإلكترونية. وسائل الاتصال. البريد الإلكتروني. السجلات الإلكترونية. | Name the contractual communication channels (e-mail addresses, platforms, e-signature tool) in the contract; under the draft Regulations that designation makes the resulting electronic records probative without further authentication. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
50:| Art. 56; Regs Arts. 265–284 | The Minister, in coordination with the Council, issues the rules on expert evidence before the court (engagement and selection, fees and expenses, duties and powers, supervision, court expert departments). Draft Regulations: a party may seek leave to use an expert (stating the field, question, cost estimate and proposed name); where parties agree, a single joint expert may be ordered, the court considering value, complexity and speed; a five-day fast opinion is available; the competent administration manages appointment and deposits, and non-deposit can forfeit the right to expert evidence; the expert must disclose relationships and interests, act impartially, keep confidentiality and flag questions outside competence; the report is due within 60 days of the start date, extendable once by 30 days, otherwise replacement with refund; parties may put written questions once within 15 days; the expert's opinion does not bind the court, which must give reasons for departing from it; a party who relies on an expert report allows the other party to rely on it too. | يصدر الوزير - بالتنسيق مع المجلس - القواعد الخاصة بالخبرة أمام المحكمة. / يجب ألا يزيد ميعاد إيداع التقرير على ستين يوماً من التاريخ المحدد لبدء عمل الخبير، وإذا لم يودع الخبير تقريره في الميعاد المحدد فللمحكمة أن تمنحه أجلاً آخر لا يزيد على ثلاثين يوماً. / رأي الخبير لا يقيد المحكمة. | Technical and quantum disputes (SaaS SLA credits, construction accounts, valuation) almost always go to a court-appointed expert; budget 60–90 days and the deposit. A contractual agreement to a named expert or to accept an expert determination is honoured between merchants (Regs Art. 11(d)). Separate ministerial expert rules exist and were not read. `[model knowledge — verify]` | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
51:| Art. 57; Regs Art. 285 | Absent a special text or contrary agreement, commercial custom or the course of dealing between the parties may be relied on; the party invoking custom or usage must prove it. The court relies on settled commercial custom and may seek assistance to establish it when disputed. | فيما لم يرد فيه نص خاص، أو اتفاق بين الأطراف على غيره؛ يجوز الاستناد إلى العرف التجاري، أو العادة بين الأطراف. وعلى من يتمسك بالعرف أو العادة أن يثبت وجودهما. | Express contract terms displace custom; a party relying on "industry practice" (e.g. renewal or notice customs) bears the burden of proving it. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
52:| Arts. 58–66; Regs Arts. 178–209 | Pleadings close when the parties have presented their case; reopening only by reasoned decision; supplementary memoranda may be allowed (draft Regulations: within 10 days, one per party, no new claims, evidence or attachments). Deliberation is secret; judgments issue at least by majority with dissent reasons recorded; the reasoned draft is deposited at pronouncement; pronouncement in public session, adjournable once; a date for delivery of the judgment copy is set within 20 days of pronouncement (draft Regulations: 10 days absent special text). The judgment must state the court, date, circuit and judges, the parties, a summary of facts, claims and material pleas, and the reasons and operative part (insufficient factual reasoning voids the judgment, Regs Art. 193); the enforceable copy bears the enforcement formula and is delivered only to the party with an interest in enforcement. Draft Regulations require the merits judgment to decide the claim for material and moral damages including litigation costs, weighing the harm, the amount awarded, the debtor's procrastination, custom and any expert opinion. The issuing court handles correction and interpretation. | تكون المداولة في الأحكام سرًّا بين القضاة ... تصدر الأحكام بالأغلبية على الأقل. / ويجب أن يحدد - بعد النطق بالحكم - موعدٌ لتسليم صورة من نسخته، على أن يكون التسليم خلال مدة لا تتجاوز (عشرين) يوماً من تاريخ النطق به. / يجب على المحكمة أن تضمن حكمها في الموضوع الفصل في طلب التعويض عن الأضرار المادية والمعنوية بما في ذلك مصاريف التقاضي. | The appeal clock runs from the date fixed for delivery of the judgment copy, not from pronouncement (Art. 79). Litigation costs and lawyers' fees are recoverable only as a damages claim that must be pleaded; there is no automatic costs-follow-the-event rule in the Law. Court filing fees under the Judicial Costs Law (نظام التكاليف القضائية) are a separate regime not read for this file. `[model knowledge — verify]` | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
53:| Art. 65; Regs Arts. 202–205 | Judgments and orders are immediately enforceable (التنفيذ المعجل) when issued in an urgent case or as payment orders; on the judgment creditor's request the court may order immediate enforcement where delay would cause serious harm, or where the judgment rests on an acknowledgment or on a private document the debtor did not deny. Draft Regulations: statutory immediate enforcement applies even if the judgment is silent; the court may require security; the appeal court may stay immediate enforcement where the grounds of appeal may lead to reversal and serious harm is feared. | تكون الأحكام أو الأوامر مشمولة بالتنفيذ المعجل في الحالات الآتية: إذا كان الحكم أو الأمر صادراً في دعوى مستعجلة. أوامر الأداء بموجب أحكام النظام. للمحكمة - بناءً على طلب المحكوم له - أن تقرر شمول الحكم بالتنفيذ المعجل ... أن يترتب على تأخير التنفيذ ضرر جسيم ... أن يكون الحكم مبنيًّا على الإقرار بالحق، أو مبنيًّا على ورقة عادية لم ينكرها المحكوم عليه. | Ordinary money judgments are not enforceable until final (the 30-day appeal period has run or appeal is exhausted); the Enforcement Law's list of instruments covers "final judgments and judgments covered by immediate enforcement" (see `enforcement-law.md`, Art. 7(1)(a)). Ask for immediate enforcement where the claim rests on an undenied invoice or acknowledgment. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
54:| Arts. 67–71; Regs Arts. 210–228 | By exception to ordinary filing, a creditor may apply for a payment order (أمر أداء) where the right is established in writing, the debt is due, and it is a determinate sum of money or fungible/specific movable; the creditor must first demand payment in writing at least five days before applying, stating the intended application date; the circuit decides within 10 days of registration, refusal being final without prejudice to an ordinary action; the debtor may lodge a grievance (تظلم) before the competent court within 15 days of service, by ordinary claim procedure and stating reasons; the court may stay immediate enforcement on reasoned decision where serious harm is feared. Draft Regulations: the sum is "determinate" if fixed on established bases leaving no discretion to the court; not available where the debtor resides outside the Kingdom, nor for reciprocal obligations unless the creditor attaches written proof of its own performance; venue is the debtor's residence; the application does not bar precautionary measures; the demand is proved through a postal or licensed electronic service provider; the debtor may also appeal for formal defects; the grievance reopens the merits within its scope. | للدائن التقدم إلى المحكمة بطلب إصدار أمر بأداء دين بالشروط الآتية: أن يكون حقه ثابتاً بالكتابة. أن يكون الدين حالَّ الأداء. أن يكون الدين معين المقدار ... يجب أن يشعر الدائن المدين - كتابةً - بطلب الوفاء قبل (خمسة) أيام على الأقل ... تفصل الدائرة في الطلب بأمر تصدره خلال (عشرة) أيام من تاريخ قيده ... يجوز للمدين التظلم من أمر الأداء ... خلال (خمسة عشر) يوماً من تاريخ إبلاغه. | For undisputed invoices, signed acknowledgments or written debt instruments against a Saudi-resident debtor, the payment order is the fastest route to an immediately enforceable title (Art. 65(1)(b)). Not usable against a foreign debtor under the draft Regulations. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
55:| Art. 74; Regs Arts. 288–290 | Only the losing party, or a party not awarded all its claims, may object; the parties may agree, even before the claim is filed, that the first-instance judgment is final; objections to interlocutory judgments go with the objection to the merits judgment, except that judgments on staying the case, jurisdiction, hearing of the claim, **the plea of an arbitration clause**, and temporary and urgent judgments may be objected to before the merits judgment; objection to an immediately enforceable judgment does not stay it; the objector is not prejudiced by its own objection. Draft Regulations: a finality agreement cannot bind one party only; it must be invoked before any request or defence on appeal; an objector may waive the objection. | يجوز الاتفاق - ولو قبل رفع الدعوى - على أن يكون حكم الدائرة الابتدائية نهائيًّا. / ويجوز الاعتراض على الحكم الصادر في وقف الدعوى، أو الاختصاص، أو سماع الدعوى، أو الدفع بشرط التحكيم، وعلى الأحكام الوقتية والمستعجلة، قبل الحكم في الموضوع. | A mutual "no appeal" clause in a commercial contract is valid and removes the appeal tier; use it deliberately. A refusal to dismiss in favour of arbitration can be appealed immediately rather than after a full trial. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
56:| Art. 77; Regs Art. 206 | Final judgments that have acquired res judicata are conclusive as to what they decided, but only in a dispute between the same parties in the same capacities concerning the same right, subject and cause; the court applies this of its own motion. Reasons acquire res judicata only where inseparably linked to the operative part. | الأحكام النهائية - التي حازت حجية الأمر المقضي - حجةٌ فيما فصلت فيه من الخصومة ... وتقضي المحكمة بهذه الحجية من تلقاء نفسها. | Findings in a prior Saudi commercial judgment between the same parties bind a later case on the same right; findings against different parties or on different causes do not. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
57:| Arts. 78–79; Regs Arts. 294, 303–312 | All first-instance judgments and decisions are appealable except small claims not exceeding SAR 50,000 as determined by the Council (draft Regulations: unless the judgment was on jurisdiction, inadmissibility, non-hearing for lapse of time, formal non-acceptance, or a preliminary plea barring the case); the Council determines which appeals are decided without a hearing (draft Regulations: judgments in Art. 16(1)–(3) claims not exceeding SAR 2m, Art. 16(8)–(9) claims, and matters within the single-judge appeal circuit). **The appeal period is 30 days from the date fixed for delivery of the judgment copy; 10 days for judgments on jurisdiction and in urgent cases**, the latter being referred the next day and decided within five working days; a final judgment on subject-matter or territorial jurisdiction is not open to any objection. | تكون المهلة المحددة للاستئناف على الأحكام (ثلاثين) يوماً من التاريخ المحدد لتسليم صورة نسخة الحكم. تكون المهلة المحددة للاستئناف على الأحكام الصادرة في الاختصاص وعلى الأحكام الصادرة في الدعاوى المستعجلة، (عشرة) أيام. / لا يقبل الحكم النهائي الصادر في اختصاص المحكمة نوعيًّا أو مكانيًّا الاعتراضَ بأي طريق. | Diary the copy-delivery date, not the hearing date. Most mid-value contract appeals (≤ SAR 2m) are decided on the papers if the draft Regulations stand. Small claims under SAR 50,000 are single-tier. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
58:| Arts. 80–85; Regs Arts. 296–302 | A single-judge appeal circuit hears objections to single-judge urgent decisions, payment orders, judgments ending or abandoning the case, and other matters the Council designates. Appeal is by petition stating the judgment, grounds and requests (missing elements mean non-acceptance under the draft Regulations); it transfers the case as it stood, limited to what is appealed, and the court may admit new evidence, pleas and defences but **not new claims** (except increased compensation, profits or rent accruing after the final submissions); the respondent may cross-appeal until closing of pleadings; an absent appellant risks the appeal being deemed not brought after one adjournment of up to 30 days; on reversal the case is remitted for alternative claims or, where dismissed on a preliminary ground, for the merits. | ينقل الاستئناف الدعوى بحالتها التي كانت عليها قبل صدور الحكم المستأنف بالنسبة إلى ما رُفع عنه الاستئناف فقط ... لا تُقبل الطلبات الجديدة في الاستئناف، وتحكم محكمة الاستئناف من تلقاء نفسها بعدم قبولـها. | Frame every head of claim at first instance; new claims are inadmissible on appeal though new evidence may be admitted. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
59:| Arts. 86–92; Regs Arts. 313–321 | Reconsideration (التماس إعادة النظر) of final judgments is available in the cases set by the Law of Civil Procedure, by petition to the court that issued the final judgment (draft Regulations: the appeal circuit that affirmed it; no stay unless ordered for irreparable harm, possibly against security). Cassation before the Commercial Chamber of the Supreme Court lies against appeal-circuit judgments for: violation or misapplication of Sharia or the laws, or of a Supreme Court judicial principle; lack of jurisdiction or improper constitution; error in characterising the facts; or conflict with a prior judgment between the same parties (draft Regulations: only if that prior judgment is final). Cassation does not stay enforcement unless the court so orders on request for irreparable effects (security may be required); a reporting judge screens the petition; on cassation the case is remitted to a differently constituted panel bound by the Supreme Court's principle, or decided by the Supreme Court if ripe, and must be decided by it on a second cassation. | تختص الدائرة التجارية في المحكمة العليا بالنظر في الاعتراضات على الأحكام والقرارات التي تصدرها دوائر الاستئناف في المحكمة ... مخالفة أحكام الشريعة الإسلامية أو الأنظمة، أو الخطأ في تطبيقها أو تأويلها، أو مخالفة مبدأ قضائي صادر من المحكمة العليا. | Cassation is a legal-error review, not a third instance; appeal-circuit judgments are enforceable immediately absent a stay. Budget for enforcement risk while cassation is pending. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
60:| Art. 8(3); Regs Arts. 322–340 | The Regulations define small claims (الدعاوى اليسيرة), their procedure and judgment. Draft Regulations: small claims are the single-judge cases under Regs Arts. 17–18 (Art. 16(1) claims up to SAR 500,000, Art. 16(2) claims up to SAR 1m, related Art. 16(8)–(9) claims) except construction-contracting claims; decided within 90 days of registration (30 days where pre-filing exchange took place), entirely electronically and remotely unless the circuit decides otherwise, after conciliation not exceeding 15 days; the defendant is served the day of registration with a pre-trial meeting within 15 days; the defence is due one day before that meeting; no claims, evidence or pleas after the pre-trial meeting; expert reports within 20 days (+10); a single hearing (adjournment ≤ 15 days); judgment pronounced within five days of closing and delivered at once or within five days; appeal decided within 15 days of referral unless heard. Draft Regs Art. 17 also sets the single-judge first-instance circuit: Art. 16(1) claims up to SAR 500,000, Art. 16(2) claims up to SAR 1m, and a "requests and orders" circuit for urgent requests and payment orders; Regs Art. 18 lists the single-judge appeal matters. | يقصد بالدعاوى اليسيرة المنصوص عليها في الفقرة (3) من المادة الثامنة من النظام الدعاوى المنصوص عليها في المادتين السابعة عشرة والثامنة عشرة من اللائحة عدا الدعاوى الناشئة عن مقاولات الإنشاءات. / لا تتجاوز مدة النظر في الدعاوى اليسيرة تسعين يوماً من تاريخ القيد إلا للضرورة. | Two different "small claims" concepts coexist: the Law's SAR 50,000 non-appealability line (Art. 78) and the draft Regulations' broader single-judge fast track (up to SAR 500,000 / 1m). Do not conflate them; confirm which the approved regulation adopted. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` (Art. 8) / `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text) |
61:| Art. 8(2); Regs Arts. 341–351 | The Regulations set the class-action (الدعاوى الجماعية) procedure. Draft Regulations: unity of subject and cause, same defendant, a common objective criterion, at least ten consenting claimants, and a lawyer as representative; leave from the court president within ten days (final), with up to 60 days to reach the headcount; one statement of claim within ten days of leave with a schedule of claims; a public register; the court may appoint an adviser, classify the claimants and allow joinder until closing of pleadings. | يشترط لاعتبار المطالبات دعوى جماعية ... اتحاد موضوع المطالبة والسبب ... موافقة مدعين لا يقل عددهم عن عشرة ... تعيين ممثل للمدعين؛ على أن يكون الممثل محامياً. | Consumer- or investor-type group claims against a company can be aggregated; diligence on a target with many similar customer complaints should flag class-action exposure. | `[authority — MoJ]` (Regs, draft text; `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` for Art. 8(2) `[BOE — Arabic]`) |
62:| Art. 93; Art. 96; Decree ¶2–¶4 | Where the Law is silent, the Law of Civil Procedure applies to cases within the court's jurisdiction insofar as compatible with the commercial nature of the case. The Law entered into force 60 days after publication and repeals conflicting provisions; commercial circuits in general courts serve regions without a commercial court, with appeal to the nearest commercial court; Art. 35 of the Law of Civil Procedure (the former commercial-jurisdiction rule) is repealed. | فيما لم يرد فيه نص خاص في النظام، تطبق أحكام نظام المرافعات الشرعية على الدعاوى التي تختص بنظرها المحكمة بما لا يخالف طبيعة الدعوى التجارية. / يعمل بالنظام بعد (ستين) يوماً من تاريخ نشره في الجريدة الرسمية. | Gaps (joinder, intervention, recusal, letters rogatory) are filled from the Law of Civil Procedure, which is not in this folder. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` |
     1	# Commercial Contracts Practice Profile (test fixture, synthetic)
     2	
     3	## Who we are
     4	
     5	Example Telematics Co. is a limited liability company. The contracts team is 2 people. The Legal Lead is the final escalation point. We process roughly 15 agreements per month, mostly purchasing. We use no CLM system.
     6	**Commercial registration:** CR 1010000000 (synthetic)
     7	**Legal form:** LLC under the Companies Law
     8	**Practice setting:** In-house
     9	
    10	## Who's using this
    11	
    12	**Role:** Non-lawyer with attorney access
    13	**Attorney contact:** External Saudi counsel on retainer (synthetic)
    14	**Local counsel for escalation:** N/A for these tests
    15	
    16	## Jurisdiction
    17	
    18	**Primary jurisdiction:** `ksa`
    19	**Footprint (other jurisdictions this practice operates in):** none
    20	**Authoritative language of the primary jurisdiction:** Arabic
    21	**Output language:** English plus the authoritative language for the bottom line, findings table, and counterparty-facing text (bilingual)
    22	**Calendar for deadlines:** Friday-Saturday weekend; Eid al-Fitr, Eid al-Adha, National Day (23 September), Founding Day (22 February); Hijri dates on official instruments
    23	**Currency for thresholds:** SAR
    24	**Primary-source portal:** https://laws.boe.gov.sa
    25	**Local counsel available for escalation:** N/A
    26	**Jurisdiction playbook defaults accepted:** all rows of `references/jurisdictions/ksa/playbook-defaults.md` accepted as written
    27	
    28	**Unpopulated jurisdiction rule.** If any code above resolves to a manifest with `populated: no`, every skill stops for that code and says so.
    29	
    30	## Available integrations
    31	
    32	| Integration | Status | Fallback if unavailable |
    33	|---|---|---|
    34	| CLM | ✗ | Manual record-keeping; renewal-tracker runs against a local register |
    35	| E-signature | ✗ | User routes for signature outside the plugin |
    36	| Document storage | ✗ | User uploads agreements directly |
    37	| Slack | ✗ | Alerts delivered inline |
    38	
    39	## Playbook
    40	
    41	**Active side:** purchasing
    42	
    43	### Purchasing-side playbook
    44	
    45	#### Limitation of liability
    46	**Direct cap (multiple of fees):** Vendor cap at 12 months fees paid or payable
    47	**Indirect / consequential damages:** excluded both ways
    48	**Carveouts we require (above the cap):** Gross negligence, fraud, breach of confidentiality, data breach
    49	**Cap base definition we accept:** fees paid in the 12 months preceding the claim
    50	**Never accept:** Uncapped indirect damages; vendor exclusion of liability for gross negligence or fraud
    51	
    52	#### Indemnification
    53	**Standard position:** Vendor indemnifies for IP infringement and data breach; we indemnify for our data
    54	
    55	#### Data protection
    56	**Standard position:** Vendor signs our data-processing terms as processor
    57	**Requirements:** ISO 27001 or equivalent for any vendor touching customer data
    58	
    59	#### Term and termination
    60	**Standard position:** Termination for convenience on 30 days' notice; auto-renewal only with a 30-day cancel window
    61	**Never accept:** Multi-year lock-in with no termination rights
    62	
    63	#### Governing law and venue
    64	**Preferred:** Laws of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia
    65	**Acceptable:** English law with arbitration
    66	**Escalate:** Any foreign court jurisdiction clause
    67	**Never:** Foreign law with foreign courts and no arbitration
    68	**Forum:** arbitration
    69	**Arbitration institution and seat:** SCCA, Riyadh
    70	**Language of proceedings and prevailing contract language:** English; Arabic prevails in a Saudi forum
    71	**Jurisdiction playbook defaults applied:** all Commercial rows accepted
    72	
    73	#### The one thing
    74	Any clause letting the vendor use our fleet data for its own purposes.
    75	
    76	## Escalation
    77	
    78	| Can approve | Without escalation | Escalates to | Via |
    79	|---|---|---|---|
    80	| Contracts manager | Standard terms, under SAR 200,000 | Legal Lead | email |
    81	| Legal Lead | Under SAR 2,000,000 | CFO | email |
    82	
    83	**Value thresholds (in the profile currency, see `## Jurisdiction`):** SAR 200,000 / SAR 2,000,000
    84	**Automatic escalations regardless of contract value:** Uncapped liability, foreign courts, data use for training
    85	
    86	## House style
    87	
    88	**Tone in redlines:** Firm, courteous
    89	**Stakeholder summaries:** Procurement lead reads them; one page
    90	**Where work product goes:** Local folder
    91	**Renewal alerts go to:** email
    92	
    93	## Review preferences
    94	
    95	confirm_routing: false
    96	
    97	## NDA triage preferences
    98	
    99	closing_action: "Forward this output and the NDA to the Legal Lead."

