The source check caught a material error in the local data-protection reference: SDAIA’s Arabic regulation concerns the controller’s approval for mandatory disclosure, while the reference says the data subject’s consent. I’ll use the retrieved Arabic wording. I also confirmed that the new Enforcement Law is not yet effective on the requested review date, so its procedures will not be applied.

exec
/bin/zsh -lc "python3 -B - <<'PY'
from pathlib import Path
for name,lo,hi in [('civil-transactions-law.md',68,70),('personal-data-protection-law.md',34,45),('electronic-transactions-law.md',43,55),('arbitration-law.md',48,66)]:
 print(name)
 for i,l in enumerate((Path('references/jurisdictions/ksa')/name).read_text().splitlines(),1):
  if lo<=i<=hi:
   c=l.split('|')
   if len(c)>5: print(str(i)+': '+' | '.join([c[1],c[2],c[-2]]))
   else: print(str(i)+': '+l)
print('CALCULATIONS')
a=1800000;t=a*3;q=a/4;w=t*.10
print(dict(annual=a,total=t,quarter=q,delay_one_week=w,delay_two_weeks=2*w,cap_fraction_annual=100000/a,interest_quarter_one_year=q*.08))
PY" in /Users/basimkhoja/Projects/Legal Consultant
