**2. Deal-breaker check — PRESENT**

The [practice profile’s “one thing”](</private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-basimkhoja-Projects-Legal-Consultant/a0531e0a-683c-4903-92eb-1e4e392ffe61/scratchpad/homes/ksa/commercial-legal/CLAUDE.md:73>) prohibits:

> “Any clause letting the vendor use our fleet data for its own purposes.”

Clause 7 does exactly that. Product improvement is sufficient to trigger this prohibition; proof of AI training is unnecessary. The draft does **not** expressly mention training, so the separate training escalation trigger is not treated as an established fact.

The available positions are removal of the permission or no signature if Vendor refuses. No documented fallback permits anonymised, aggregated, or otherwise repurposed fleet data.

